window.SOURATE_DATA = {"numSourate":20,"nomSourate":"Taha","nomFr":"Ta-Ha","nomEn":"Ta-Ha","nomArabe":"طه","lieu":"La Mecque","lieuEn":"Makkah","typeSourateLabel":"Sourate Mecquoise","typeSourateLabelEn":"Meccan Surah","typeSourateClasse":"mecquoise","ordreRev":45,"nbVersets":135,"versets":[{"numVerset":1,"texteArabe":"بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيمِ طه","tradPropre":"Tâ-Hâ.","tradEn":"Ṭā, Hā.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ṭâ-Hâ: Ces lettres isolées placées en ouverture de la sourate appartiennent au secret d'Allāh et démontrent le miracle inimitable du Coran, composé des mêmes lettres arabes que celles utilisées par les hommes.","explicationEn":"1. This sūrah begins with the disconnected letters, the explanation for which has already preceeded in Sūrah Baqarah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020001","lienPrecedent":"sourate-19-verset-98.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-2.html"},{"numVerset":2,"texteArabe":"مَا أَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْقُرْآنَ لِتَشْقَىٰ","tradPropre":"Nous n'avons point fait descendre sur toi le Coran pour que tu sois malheureux,","tradEn":"We have not sent down to you the Qur’ān that you be distressed","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, Nous ne t’avons pas révélé le Coran pour que le refus des tiens de croire en toi t’abatte moralement.","explicationEn":"2. I have not revealed the Qur’ān to you, O Messenger, to become distressed by your people’s turning away from having faith in it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020002","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-1.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-3.html"},{"numVerset":3,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا تَذْكِرَةً لِمَنْ يَخْشَىٰ","tradPropre":"si ce n'est qu'un Rappel pour celui qui redoute (Allah),","tradEn":"But only as a reminder for those who fear [Allāh] -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous ne l’avons révélé que pour qu’il soit un rappel adressé à ceux à qui Il a facilité de Le craindre.","explicationEn":"3. We only revealed it to be a reminder for those whom Allah has blessed so that they fear Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020003","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-2.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-4.html"},{"numVerset":4,"texteArabe":"تَنْزِيلًا مِمَّنْ خَلَقَ الْأَرْضَ وَالسَّمَاوَاتِ الْعُلَى","tradPropre":"(et comme) une révélation émanant de Celui qui a créé la terre et les cieux sublimes.","tradEn":"A revelation from He who created the earth and highest heavens,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est Allah, le Créateur de la Terre et des très haut Cieux, qui te l’a révélé. Il s’agit d’un Livre éminent puisque révélé par l’Etre Suprême","explicationEn":"4. It was sent down by Allah, Who created the earth and the high heavens. It is thus a grand Qur’ān, as it was sent down by a Grand Being.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020004","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-3.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-5.html"},{"numVerset":5,"texteArabe":"الرَّحْمَانُ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ اسْتَوَىٰ","tradPropre":"Le Tout Miséricordieux S'est établi «Istawâ» sur le Trône.","tradEn":"The Most Merciful [who is] above the Throne established.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le Tout Miséricordieux s’est élevé, d’une manière qui sied à Sa Majesté, au-dessus du Trône.","explicationEn":"5. The Merciful who established Himself on the Throne, in a meaning that is befitting for His Majesty, may He be glorified.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020005","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-4.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-6.html"},{"numVerset":6,"texteArabe":"لَهُ مَا فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَا فِي الْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَمَا تَحْتَ الثَّرَىٰ","tradPropre":"A Lui appartient ce qui est dans les cieux, sur la terre, ce qui est entre eux et ce qui est sous le sol humide.","tradEn":"To Him belongs what is in the heavens and what is on the earth and what is between them and what is under the soil.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"A Lui, exalté soit-Il, revient la possession de ce que contiennent les Cieux et la Terre ainsi que toutes les créatures vivant sous terre. Il crée, possède et se charge de gérer tout cela.","explicationEn":"6. Everything in the heavens and on earth, and all that is beneath the soil, belong to Him alone, may He be glorified. He created, owns and controls all of it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020006","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-5.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-7.html"},{"numVerset":7,"texteArabe":"وَإِنْ تَجْهَرْ بِالْقَوْلِ فَإِنَّهُ يَعْلَمُ السِّرَّ وَأَخْفَى","tradPropre":"Et si tu élèves la voix, Il connaît certes les secrets, même les plus cachés.","tradEn":"And if you speak aloud - then indeed, He knows the secret and what is [even] more hidden.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, que tu manifestes tes pensées ou les dissimules, Allah les connaîtra car Il connaît ce qui est secret et ce qui est encore plus dissimulé que les secrets, comme l’état d’esprit d’une personne par exemple, et rien ne Lui échappe.","explicationEn":"7. If you, O Messenger, proclaim the word or conceal it, He, may He be glorified, knows all of that. He knows the secrets and what is even more hidden, such as thoughts in the mind. Nothing is hidden from Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020007","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-6.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-8.html"},{"numVerset":8,"texteArabe":"اللَّهُ لَا إِلَاهَ إِلَّا هُوَ  لَهُ الْأَسْمَاءُ الْحُسْنَىٰ","tradPropre":"Allah! Point de divinité que Lui! Il possède les noms les plus beaux.","tradEn":"Allāh - there is no deity except Him. To Him belong the best names.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il n’existe pas de divinité méritant d’être adorée hormis Allah et c’est Lui Seul qui détient les Plus Beaux Noms.","explicationEn":"8. Allah, there is no being deserving of worship besides Him. To Him alone belong the perfect Names that have reached the most complete level of perfection and excellence.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020008","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-7.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-9.html"},{"numVerset":9,"texteArabe":"وَهَلْ أَتَاكَ حَدِيثُ مُوسَىٰ","tradPropre":"Le récit de Moïse t'est-il parvenu?","tradEn":"And has the story of Moses reached you? -","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Moïse qui, en provenance de Madian, se dirigeait vers l’Egypte qu’il avait dû quitter dix années auparavant après avoir tué involontairement un Egyptien.","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, connais-tu le récit de Moïse?","explicationEn":"9. The story of Moses, son of Imran, (peace be upon him), has come to you - O Messenger.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020009","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-8.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-10.html"},{"numVerset":10,"texteArabe":"إِذْ رَأَىٰ نَارًا فَقَالَ لِأَهْلِهِ امْكُثُوا إِنِّي آنَسْتُ نَارًا لَعَلِّي آتِيكُمْ مِنْهَا بِقَبَسٍ أَوْ أَجِدُ عَلَى النَّارِ هُدًى","tradPropre":"Lorsqu'il vit du feu, il dit à sa famille: «Restez ici! Je vois du feu de loin; peut-être vous en apporterai-je un tison, ou trouverai-je auprès du feu de quoi me guider».","tradEn":"When he saw a fire and said to his family, \"Stay here; indeed, I have perceived a fire; perhaps I can bring you a torch or find at the fire some guidance.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Il s’était en effet égaré.","explicationUnanime":"Lorsqu’il aperçut un feu durant son voyage, il dit à sa famille: Restez ici! J’ai aperçu un feu au loin. Peut-être que je vous apporterai de quoi allumer un foyer ou trouverai-je quelqu’un qui puisse me montrer mon chemin.","explicationEn":"10. When he saw a fire whilst travelling and he said to his family: Stay here––I can see a fire. Maybe I can bring you a flaming brand from it or find somebody to guide me to the path.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020010","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-9.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-11.html"},{"numVerset":11,"texteArabe":"فَلَمَّا أَتَاهَا نُودِيَ يَا مُوسَىٰ","tradPropre":"Puis, lorsqu'il y arriva, il fut interpellé: «Moïse!","tradEn":"And when he came to it, he was called, \"O Moses,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Arrivé près du feu, Allah l’appela: O Moïse!","explicationEn":"11. When he came to the fire, Allah, may He be glorified, called out to him saying: O Moses.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020011","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-10.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-12.html"},{"numVerset":12,"texteArabe":"إِنِّي أَنَا رَبُّكَ فَاخْلَعْ نَعْلَيْكَ  إِنَّكَ بِالْوَادِ الْمُقَدَّسِ طُوًى","tradPropre":"Je suis ton Seigneur. Enlève tes sandales: car tu es dans la vallée sacrée, Tuwâ.","tradEn":"Indeed, I am your Lord, so remove your sandals. Indeed, you are in the blessed valley of Ṭuwā.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est Moi ton Seigneur. Déchausse-toi avant de converser avec Moi. Tu es dans la vallée pure nommée Ṭuwâ.","explicationEn":"12. I am your Lord. Take off your shoes in preparation for your conversation with me. You are in the purified valley (of Tuwa.)","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020012","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-11.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-13.html"},{"numVerset":13,"texteArabe":"وَأَنَا اخْتَرْتُكَ فَاسْتَمِعْ لِمَا يُوحَىٰ","tradPropre":"Moi, Je t'ai choisi. Ecoute donc ce qui va être révélé.","tradEn":"And I have chosen you, so listen to what is revealed [to you].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Moïse, c’est Moi qui t’ai choisi afin de transmettre Mon Message. Ecoute donc ce qui t’es révélé.","explicationEn":"13. I have chosen you - O Moses - to convey My message, so listen to what I reveal to you.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020013","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-12.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-14.html"},{"numVerset":14,"texteArabe":"إِنَّنِي أَنَا اللَّهُ لَا إِلَاهَ إِلَّا أَنَا فَاعْبُدْنِي وَأَقِمِ الصَّلَاةَ لِذِكْرِي","tradPropre":"Certes, c'est Moi Allah: point de divinité que Moi. Adore-Moi donc et accomplis la Salât pour te souvenir de Moi.","tradEn":"Indeed, I am Allāh. There is no deity except Me, so worship Me and establish prayer for My remembrance.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Je suis Allah, il n’existe pas de divinité digne d’être adorée en dehors de Moi. Adore-Moi Seul et accomplis la prière de manière complète afin de M’évoquer par cette adoration.","explicationEn":"14. I am Allah; there is no being deserving of worship but Me. So worship Me alone and perform the prayer in the perfect manner so that you may remember Me in it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020014","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-13.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-15.html"},{"numVerset":15,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ السَّاعَةَ آتِيَةٌ أَكَادُ أُخْفِيهَا لِتُجْزَىٰ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ بِمَا تَسْعَىٰ","tradPropre":"L'Heure va certes arriver. Je la cache à peine, pour que chaque âme soit rétribuée selon ses efforts.","tradEn":"Indeed, the Hour is coming - I almost conceal it - so that every soul may be recompensed according to that for which it strives.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Mais dont Je les ai informés afin qu’ils s’y préparent, sans toutefois leur préciser le jour de son avènement que Je tiens soigneusement secret.","explicationUnanime":"L’Heure surviendra indubitablement. Certes, Je garde secret le moment où elle aura lieu mais les gens en connaissent les indices que le Prophète leur a mentionné. Elle aura lieu afin que chacun d’eux soit rétribué pour le bien ou le mal qu’il aura fait.","explicationEn":"15. The Hour is most definitely coming and it will certainly occur. I almost keep it hidden so that no creation knows its time, but they are aware of its signs by the information given to them by the Prophet sent to them, so that each soul is rewarded for what it did, whether good or evil.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020015","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-14.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-16.html"},{"numVerset":16,"texteArabe":"فَلَا يَصُدَّنَّكَ عَنْهَا مَنْ لَا يُؤْمِنُ بِهَا وَاتَّبَعَ هَوَاهُ فَتَرْدَىٰ","tradPropre":"Que celui qui n'y croit pas et qui suit sa propre passion ne t'en détourne pas. Sinon tu périras.","tradEn":"So do not let one avert you from it who does not believe in it and follows his desire, for you [then] would perish.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ne sois donc pas détourné, par les mécréants qui rejettent la réalité de l’Heure et suivent leurs passions, des bonnes œuvres que tu accomplis afin de te préparer à ce jour. Sinon, tu serais voué à la perdition.","explicationEn":"16. Do not let those disbelievers who do not believe in it and who follow their unlawful desires distract you from believing in it and preparing for it by doing righteous action and so bring you to ruin on account of it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020016","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-15.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-17.html"},{"numVerset":17,"texteArabe":"وَمَا تِلْكَ بِيَمِينِكَ يَا مُوسَىٰ","tradPropre":"Et qu'est-ce qu'il y a dans ta main droite, ô Moïse?»","tradEn":"And what is that in your right hand, O Moses?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Qu’y a-t-il dans ta main droite, ô Moïse?","explicationEn":"17. What is that in your right hand, O Moses?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020017","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-16.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-18.html"},{"numVerset":18,"texteArabe":"قَالَ هِيَ عَصَايَ أَتَوَكَّأُ عَلَيْهَا وَأَهُشُّ بِهَا عَلَىٰ غَنَمِي وَلِيَ فِيهَا مَآرِبُ أُخْرَىٰ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «C'est mon bâton sur lequel je m'appuie, qui me sert à effeuiller (les arbres) pour mes moutons et j'en fais d'autres usages».","tradEn":"He said, \"It is my staff; I lean upon it, and I bring down leaves for my sheep and I have therein other uses.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Moïse répondit: Ceci est mon bâton sur lequel je m’appuie lorsque je marche. Je m’en sers aussi pour faire tomber les feuilles des arbres afin que mes moutons s’en nourrissent et j’en fais d’autres usages encore.","explicationEn":"18. Moses (peace be upon him) said: It is my stick: I lean on it when walking, I beat down tree leaves with it for my sheep, and it has many other uses besides those I mentioned.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020018","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-17.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-19.html"},{"numVerset":19,"texteArabe":"قَالَ أَلْقِهَا يَا مُوسَىٰ","tradPropre":"[Allah lui] dit: «Jette-le, O Moïse».","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"Throw it down, O Moses.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Jette-le à terre, ordonna Allah à Moïse.","explicationEn":"19. Allah said: Throw it down, O Moses.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020019","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-18.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-20.html"},{"numVerset":20,"texteArabe":"فَأَلْقَاهَا فَإِذَا هِيَ حَيَّةٌ تَسْعَىٰ","tradPropre":"Il le jeta: et le voici un serpent qui rampait.","tradEn":"So he threw it down, and thereupon it was a snake, moving swiftly.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Moïse jeta son bâton et voici qu’il se transforma en serpent qui se déplaçait avec rapidité et vivacité.","explicationEn":"20. Moses threw it down and it turned into a snake moving swiftly.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020020","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-19.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-21.html"},{"numVerset":21,"texteArabe":"قَالَ خُذْهَا وَلَا تَخَفْ  سَنُعِيدُهَا سِيرَتَهَا الْأُولَىٰ","tradPropre":"[Allah] dit: «Saisis-le et ne crains rien: Nous le ramènerons à son premier état.","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"Seize it and fear not; We will return it to its former condition.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah dit ensuite à Moïse: Reprends ton bâton et ne sois pas apeuré par sa transformation en serpent car lorsque tu voudras le saisir, il redeviendra un bâton.","explicationEn":"21. Allah said to Moses (peace be upon him): Take hold of the stick and do not fear its having turned into a snake. When you take hold of it I will return it to its former state.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020021","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-20.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-22.html"},{"numVerset":22,"texteArabe":"وَاضْمُمْ يَدَكَ إِلَىٰ جَنَاحِكَ تَخْرُجْ بَيْضَاءَ مِنْ غَيْرِ سُوءٍ آيَةً أُخْرَىٰ","tradPropre":"Et serre ta main sous ton aisselle: elle en sortira blanche sans aucun mal, et ce sera là un autre prodige,","tradEn":"And draw in your hand to your side; it will come out white without disease - another sign,","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ta main droite sous le bras gauche.","explicationUnanime":"Puis ramène ta main sous ton aisselle et elle sortira blanche sans être atteinte par la lèpre. Ceci constituera le deuxième de Nos signes.","explicationEn":"22. Now press your hand to your side and it will come out white, without any leprosy; that is another sign for you.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020022","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-21.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-23.html"},{"numVerset":23,"texteArabe":"لِنُرِيَكَ مِنْ آيَاتِنَا الْكُبْرَى","tradPropre":"afin que Nous te fassions voir de Nos prodiges les plus importants.","tradEn":"That We may show you [some] of Our greater signs.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Moïse, Nous t’avons montré ces deux signes afin que tu sois témoin des plus grands miracles prouvant Notre pouvoir et prouvant que tu es un messager envoyé par Allah","explicationEn":"23. I have shown you these two signs - O Moses - to show you some of My greatest signs that indicate My Power and that you are a messenger sent by Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020023","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-22.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-24.html"},{"numVerset":24,"texteArabe":"اذْهَبْ إِلَىٰ فِرْعَوْنَ إِنَّهُ طَغَىٰ","tradPropre":"Rends-toi auprès de Pharaon car il a outrepassé toute limite.","tradEn":"Go to Pharaoh. Indeed, he has transgressed [i.e., tyrannized].\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Moïse, rends-toi auprès de Pharaon car il a mécru et s’est rebellé contre Allah, dépassant ainsi toute limite.","explicationEn":"24. Go - O Moses - to Pharaoh, for he has overstepped the bounds in disbelief and rebellion against Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020024","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-23.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-25.html"},{"numVerset":25,"texteArabe":"قَالَ رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِي صَدْرِي","tradPropre":"[Moïse] dit: «Seigneur, ouvre-moi ma poitrine,","tradEn":"[Moses] said, \"My Lord, expand [i.e., relax] for me my breast [with assurance]","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Moïse demanda à Allah: Ô Seigneur, rends-moi plus tolérant aux offenses.","explicationEn":"25. Moses (peace be upon him) said: Lord, expand my breast for me so that I can bear the difficulty.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020025","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-24.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-26.html"},{"numVerset":26,"texteArabe":"وَيَسِّرْ لِي أَمْرِي","tradPropre":"et facilite ma mission,","tradEn":"And ease for me my task","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Facilite ma tâche.","explicationEn":"26. Make my task easy.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020026","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-25.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-27.html"},{"numVerset":27,"texteArabe":"وَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِنْ لِسَانِي","tradPropre":"et dénoue un nœud en ma langue,","tradEn":"And untie the knot from my tongue","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Rends-moi capable de parler sans défaut d’élocution.","explicationEn":"27. Give me the ability to speak eloquently.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020027","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-26.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-28.html"},{"numVerset":28,"texteArabe":"يَفْقَهُوا قَوْلِي","tradPropre":"afin qu'ils comprennent mes paroles,","tradEn":"That they may understand my speech.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Afin qu’ils comprennent le Message que je leur transmets.","explicationEn":"28. So that they understand my speech when I convey Your message to them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020028","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-27.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-29.html"},{"numVerset":29,"texteArabe":"وَاجْعَلْ لِي وَزِيرًا مِنْ أَهْلِي","tradPropre":"et assigne-moi un assistant de ma famille:","tradEn":"And appoint for me a minister [i.e., assistant] from my family -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Donne-moi pour aide quelqu’un de ma famille afin qu’il m’assiste dans ma mission.","explicationEn":"29. Give me a helper from my family who will assist me in my affairs.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020029","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-28.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-30.html"},{"numVerset":30,"texteArabe":"هَارُونَ أَخِي","tradPropre":"Aaron, mon frère,","tradEn":"Aaron, my brother.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Que cet aide soit mon frère, Aaron fils de ‘Imrân.","explicationEn":"30. Aaron, the son of Imran, my brother.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020030","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-29.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-31.html"},{"numVerset":31,"texteArabe":"اشْدُدْ بِهِ أَزْرِي","tradPropre":"accrois par lui ma force!","tradEn":"Increase through him my strength","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Protège, par lui, mes arrières.","explicationEn":"31. Strengthen my determination through him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020031","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-30.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-32.html"},{"numVerset":32,"texteArabe":"وَأَشْرِكْهُ فِي أَمْرِي","tradPropre":"et associe-le à ma mission,","tradEn":"And let him share my task","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Fais de lui mon partenaire dans la transmission du Message.","explicationEn":"32. And make him my partner in the mission.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020032","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-31.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-33.html"},{"numVerset":33,"texteArabe":"كَيْ نُسَبِّحَكَ كَثِيرًا","tradPropre":"afin que nous Te glorifions beaucoup,","tradEn":"That we may exalt You much","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Afin que Nous Te glorifiions souvent.","explicationEn":"33. So that we can glorify You much.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020033","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-32.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-34.html"},{"numVerset":34,"texteArabe":"وَنَذْكُرَكَ كَثِيرًا","tradPropre":"et que nous T'invoquions beaucoup.","tradEn":"And remember You much.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Et que Nous Te mentionnions souvent.","explicationEn":"34. And remember You much.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020034","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-33.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-35.html"},{"numVerset":35,"texteArabe":"إِنَّكَ كُنْتَ بِنَا بَصِيرًا","tradPropre":"Et Toi, certes, Tu es Très Clairvoyant sur nous».","tradEn":"Indeed, You are of us ever Seeing.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Car Tu vois tout de nous et rien ne T’échappe.","explicationEn":"35. You are always watching over us. Nothing of ours is hidden from You.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020035","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-34.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-36.html"},{"numVerset":36,"texteArabe":"قَالَ قَدْ أُوتِيتَ سُؤْلَكَ يَا مُوسَىٰ","tradPropre":"[Allah] dit: «Ta demande est exaucée, ô Moïse.","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"You have been granted your request, O Moses.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah lui répondit: Nous t’accordons ce que tu demandes, ô Moïse.","explicationEn":"36. Allah said: I have granted your request, O Moses.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020036","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-35.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-37.html"},{"numVerset":37,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ مَنَنَّا عَلَيْكَ مَرَّةً أُخْرَىٰ","tradPropre":"Et Nous t'avons déjà favorisé une première fois","tradEn":"And We had already conferred favor upon you another time,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce présent don suit un don précédent de Notre part.","explicationEn":"37. I had favoured you another time.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020037","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-36.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-38.html"},{"numVerset":38,"texteArabe":"إِذْ أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ أُمِّكَ مَا يُوحَىٰ","tradPropre":"lorsque Nous révélâmes à ta mère ce qui fut révélé:","tradEn":"When We inspired to your mother what We inspired,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Rappelle-toi que Nous avons inspiré à ta mère de te préserver contre l’intrigue de Pharaon.","explicationEn":"38. When We inspired your mother by that which was a means by which Allah protected you from Pharaoh’s plot.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020038","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-37.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-39.html"},{"numVerset":39,"texteArabe":"أَنِ اقْذِفِيهِ فِي التَّابُوتِ فَاقْذِفِيهِ فِي الْيَمِّ فَلْيُلْقِهِ الْيَمُّ بِالسَّاحِلِ يَأْخُذْهُ عَدُوٌّ لِي وَعَدُوٌّ لَهُ  وَأَلْقَيْتُ عَلَيْكَ مَحَبَّةً مِنِّي وَلِتُصْنَعَ عَلَىٰ عَيْنِي","tradPropre":"«Mets-le dans le coffret, puis jette celui-ci dans les flots pour qu'ensuite le fleuve le lance sur la rive; un ennemi à Moi et à lui le prendra». Et J'ai répandu sur toi une affection de Ma part, afin que tu sois élevé sous Mon œil.","tradEn":"[Saying], 'Cast him into the chest and cast it into the river, and the river will throw it onto the bank; there will take him an enemy to Me and an enemy to him.' And I bestowed upon you love from Me that you would be brought up under My eye [i.e., observation and care].","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Moïse, encore nourrisson, afin de le sauver des hommes de Pharaon qui, craignant l’avènement d’un Hébreu qui causerait la chute de son royaume, avait ordonné que soit tué tout nouveau-né hébreu de sexe masculin.<br><br><strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Pharaon et son entourage, notamment.","explicationUnanime":"Nous lui avons en effet inspiré de te mettre à l’eau après t’avoir mis dans un couffin. Nous ordonnerons alors à l’eau de faire échouer ce couffin sur le rivage et l’un de Nos ennemis et des ennemis du nourrisson le récupèrera. Il s’agit de Pharaon. Ô Moïse, Je t’ai enveloppé de Mon amour, ce qui amena de ce fait les gens à t’aimer, afin que tu sois élevé sous Ma garde et préservé par Ma sollicitude.","explicationEn":"39. I had instructed her when I inspired her: Throw your child after he is born into the chest and then place the chest into the river. The river will cast him on to the bank by My command, and he will be taken in by an enemy of Mine and his, who is Pharaoh. I placed on you love from Me, so that people love you, and so that you are reared under My watchful eye, protection and care.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020039","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-38.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-40.html"},{"numVerset":40,"texteArabe":"إِذْ تَمْشِي أُخْتُكَ فَتَقُولُ هَلْ أَدُلُّكُمْ عَلَىٰ مَنْ يَكْفُلُهُ  فَرَجَعْنَاكَ إِلَىٰ أُمِّكَ كَيْ تَقَرَّ عَيْنُهَا وَلَا تَحْزَنَ  وَقَتَلْتَ نَفْسًا فَنَجَّيْنَاكَ مِنَ الْغَمِّ وَفَتَنَّاكَ فُتُونًا  فَلَبِثْتَ سِنِينَ فِي أَهْلِ مَدْيَنَ ثُمَّ جِئْتَ عَلَىٰ قَدَرٍ يَا مُوسَىٰ","tradPropre":"Et vœilà que ta sœur (te suivait en) marchant et disait: «Puis-je vous indiquer quelqu'un qui se chargera de lui?» Ainsi, Nous te rapportâmes à ta mère afin que son oil se réjouisse et qu'elle ne s'afflige plus. Tu tuas ensuite un individu; Nous te sauvâmes des craintes qui t'oppressaient; et Nous t'imposâmes plusieurs épreuves. Puis tu demeuras des années durant chez les habitants de Madyan. Ensuite tu es venu, ô Moïse, conformément à un décret.","tradEn":"[And We favored you] when your sister went and said, 'Shall I direct you to someone who will be responsible for him?' So We restored you to your mother that she might be content and not grieve. And you killed someone, but We saved you from retaliation and tried you with a [severe] trial. And you remained [some] years among the people of Madyan. Then you came [here] at the decreed time, O Moses.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> A l’entourage de Pharaon qui avait recueilli l’enfant et qui était à la recherche d’une nourrice capable de l’allaiter, puisque Moïse refusait systématiquement le sein des nourrices.","explicationUnanime":"Ta sœur sortit suivre le couffin qui te contenait et dit à ceux qui te recueillirent: Voulez-vous que je vous indique des gens capables de le protéger, de l’allaiter et de l’élever? Nous t’avons alors fait la faveur de te rendre à ta mère afin qu’elle soit réjouie par ton retour et qu’elle soit moins attristée. Plus tard, tu as tué un Copte en le frappant et Nous t’avons alors fait la faveur de te sauver de la punition. C‘est ainsi que Nous t’avons sauvegardé à chaque épreuve. Par la suite, tu as vécu longtemps chez les Madyan.","explicationEn":"40. When your sister went out following the chest wherever it went, and she said to those who took it: Shall I show you someone who will take care of him, nurse him and rear him. I then favoured you by returning you to your mother so that she could rejoice by your return to her and not grieve over you. Then You killed the copt whom you punched, but We favoured you by saving you from difficulty. And we helped you time after time from every test that you faced. You then left and stayed among the people of Madyan for years, then you came at the time that was specified for you to come to be spoken to O Moses.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020040","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-39.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-41.html"},{"numVerset":41,"texteArabe":"وَاصْطَنَعْتُكَ لِنَفْسِي","tradPropre":"Et je t'ai assigné à Moi-Même.","tradEn":"And I produced you for Myself.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis Je t’ai choisi afin que tu sois le messager que J’envoie aux gens afin de transmettre ce que je Lui révèle.","explicationEn":"41. I have selected you as My messenger to convey to people the revelation I sent to you.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020041","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-40.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-42.html"},{"numVerset":42,"texteArabe":"اذْهَبْ أَنْتَ وَأَخُوكَ بِآيَاتِي وَلَا تَنِيَا فِي ذِكْرِي","tradPropre":"Pars, toi et ton frère, avec Mes prodiges; et ne négligez pas de M'invoquer.","tradEn":"Go, you and your brother, with My signs and do not slacken in My remembrance.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Moïse, pars avec ton frère Aaron accompagnés de Nos signes prouvant le pouvoir et l’Unicité d’Allah et ne faiblissez pas lorsque vous prêchez Mon Message et Me mentionnez.","explicationEn":"42. Go, you - O Moses - and your brother Aaron, with My signs indicating Allah’s Power and Oneness, and do not slacken in calling towards Me and in remembering Me.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020042","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-41.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-43.html"},{"numVerset":43,"texteArabe":"اذْهَبَا إِلَىٰ فِرْعَوْنَ إِنَّهُ طَغَىٰ","tradPropre":"Allez vers Pharaon: il s'est vraiment rebellé.","tradEn":"Go, both of you, to Pharaoh. Indeed, he has transgressed.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Rendez-vous auprès de Pharaon car sa mécréance et sa rébellion ont outrepassé les limites.","explicationEn":"43. Go to Pharaoh, for he has overstepped the bounds in disbelief and rebellion against Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020043","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-42.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-44.html"},{"numVerset":44,"texteArabe":"فَقُولَا لَهُ قَوْلًا لَيِّنًا لَعَلَّهُ يَتَذَكَّرُ أَوْ يَخْشَىٰ","tradPropre":"Puis, parlez-lui gentiment. Peut-être se rappellera-t-il ou [Me] craindra-t-il?","tradEn":"And speak to him with gentle speech that perhaps he may be reminded or fear [Allāh].\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Dites-lui des paroles douces sans agressivité, peut-être qu’il se rappellera, Me craindra et finira par se repentir.","explicationEn":"44. Speak to him gently without harshness, in the hope that he may take heed, fear Allah and repent.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020044","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-43.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-45.html"},{"numVerset":45,"texteArabe":"قَالَا رَبَّنَا إِنَّنَا نَخَافُ أَنْ يَفْرُطَ عَلَيْنَا أَوْ أَنْ يَطْغَىٰ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «O notre Seigneur, nous craignons qu'il ne nous maltraite indûment, ou qu'il dépasse les limites».","tradEn":"They said, \"Our Lord, indeed we are afraid that he will hasten [punishment] against us or that he will transgress.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Inquiets, Moïse et Aaron dirent à Allah: Nous craignons que Pharaon s’empresse de nous punir alors avant que nous ayons terminé de lui communiquer le message ou qu’il soit extrêmement injuste avec nous en nous mettant à mort ou en nous infligeant un autre supplice.","explicationEn":"45. Moses and Aaron peace be upon them) said: We fear that he will quickly punish us before we can deliver Your message to him, or that he will exceed the limit in oppressing us by killing us or otherwise.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020045","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-44.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-46.html"},{"numVerset":46,"texteArabe":"قَالَ لَا تَخَافَا  إِنَّنِي مَعَكُمَا أَسْمَعُ وَأَرَىٰ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «Ne craignez rien. Je suis avec vous: J'entends et Je vois.","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"Fear not. Indeed, I am with you both; I hear and I see.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah leur répondit: Il n’y a pas lieu d’avoir peur, car Je vous accompagne par Mon soutien et Mon assistance. J’entendrai et je verrai ce qui se produira lorsque vous serez auprès de lui.","explicationEn":"46. Allah said to them: Do not be afraid, I am with you both with My help and support. I hear and see everything that occurs between you and him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020046","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-45.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-47.html"},{"numVerset":47,"texteArabe":"فَأْتِيَاهُ فَقُولَا إِنَّا رَسُولَا رَبِّكَ فَأَرْسِلْ مَعَنَا بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ وَلَا تُعَذِّبْهُمْ  قَدْ جِئْنَاكَ بِآيَةٍ مِنْ رَبِّكَ  وَالسَّلَامُ عَلَىٰ مَنِ اتَّبَعَ الْهُدَىٰ","tradPropre":"Allez donc chez lui; puis, dites-lui: «Nous sommes tous deux, les messagers de ton Seigneur. Envoie donc les Enfants d'Israël en notre compagnie et ne les châtie plus. Nous sommes venus à toi avec une preuve de la part de ton Seigneur. Et que la paix soit sur quiconque suit le droit chemin!","tradEn":"So go to him and say, 'Indeed, we are messengers of your Lord, so send with us the Children of Israel and do not torment them. We have come to you with a sign from your Lord. And peace will be upon he who follows the guidance.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allez donc à lui et dites: Ô Pharaon, nous sommes les messagers d’Allah. Laisse donc les Israélites partir en notre compagnie et cesse de tuer leurs enfants et de réduire leurs femmes en esclavage. Nous t’avons fourni la preuve manifeste de ton Seigneur qui prouve la véracité de nos propos. Que le châtiment d’Allah soit épargné à ceux qui croient et suivent la guidée d’Allah!","explicationEn":"47. So go to him and tell him: We are the messengers of your Lord - O Pharaoh - so send the Israelites with us and do not punish them by killing their sons and letting their women live. We have brought to you a sign from your Lord proving our truthfulness. Safety from Allah’s punishment is for those who have faith and follow Allah’s guidance.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020047","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-46.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-48.html"},{"numVerset":48,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا قَدْ أُوحِيَ إِلَيْنَا أَنَّ الْعَذَابَ عَلَىٰ مَنْ كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلَّىٰ","tradPropre":"Il nous a été révélé que le châtiment est pour celui qui refuse d'avoir foi et qui tourne le dos».","tradEn":"Indeed, it has been revealed to us that the punishment will be upon whoever denies and turns away.'\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"En effet, il nous a été révélé que le châtiment s’abat dans le bas monde sur ceux qui démentent les signes d’Allah et se détournent de ce que leur apportent les messagers.","explicationEn":"48. Allah has revealed to us that punishment in this world and the afterlife falls on whoever rejects the signs of Allah and turns his back on what the messengers brought.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020048","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-47.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-49.html"},{"numVerset":49,"texteArabe":"قَالَ فَمَنْ رَبُّكُمَا يَا مُوسَىٰ","tradPropre":"Alors [Pharaon] dit: «Qui donc est votre Seigneur, ô Moïse?»","tradEn":"[Pharaoh] said, \"So who is the Lord of you two, O Moses?\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Lorsqu’ils furent en sa présence.","explicationUnanime":"Rejetant avec orgueil ce à quoi il a été invité, Pharaon dit: Ö Moïse, qui est donc ce Seigneur dont vous prétendez qu’Il vous a envoyés à moi?","explicationEn":"49. Pharaoh said, in denial of what they brought: Who then is your Lord, whom you claim has sent you to me, O Moses?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020049","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-48.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-50.html"},{"numVerset":50,"texteArabe":"قَالَ رَبُّنَا الَّذِي أَعْطَىٰ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ خَلْقَهُ ثُمَّ هَدَىٰ","tradPropre":"«Notre Seigneur, dit Moïse, est Celui qui a donné à chaque chose sa propre nature puis l'a dirigée».","tradEn":"He said, \"Our Lord is He who gave each thing its form and then guided [it].\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Autre sens : qui a attribué à chaque créature ce dont elle a besoin, tout en lui indiquant comment en tirer avantage.","explicationUnanime":"Moïse rétorqua: C’est notre Seigneur qui a donné à chaque chose l’apparence et la forme qui lui sied, puis guide les créatures vers la finalité de leur création.","explicationEn":"50. Moses said: Our Lord is the One Who gave everything the shape and form suitable for it, and then He guided all created things to what they were created for.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020050","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-49.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-51.html"},{"numVerset":51,"texteArabe":"قَالَ فَمَا بَالُ الْقُرُونِ الْأُولَىٰ","tradPropre":"«Qu'en est-il donc des générations anciennes?» dit Pharaon.","tradEn":"[Pharaoh] said, \"Then what is the case of the former generations?\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Qui, avant nous, ont renié ton Seigneur.","explicationUnanime":"Pharaon interrogea Moïse de nouveau: Quel a été le sort des peuples mécréants du passé?","explicationEn":"51. Pharaoh said: What about the previous communities who had disbelieved?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020051","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-50.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-52.html"},{"numVerset":52,"texteArabe":"قَالَ عِلْمُهَا عِنْدَ رَبِّي فِي كِتَابٍ  لَا يَضِلُّ رَبِّي وَلَا يَنْسَى","tradPropre":"Moïse dit: «La connaissance de leur sort est auprès de mon Seigneur, dans un livre. Mon Seigneur [ne commet] ni erreur ni oubli.","tradEn":"[Moses] said, \"The knowledge thereof is with my Lord in a record. My Lord neither errs nor forgets.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Moïse dit à Pharaon: C’est mon Seigneur qui détient la connaissance de ce qu’il est advenu d’eux et Il l’a consignée dans la Table Préservée. Mon Seigneur ne commet pas d’erreur dans ce qu’Il connaît et Il ne l’oublie pas.","explicationEn":"52. Moses (peace be upon him) said to Pharaoh: The knowledge of what those communities did is with my Lord, recorded in the Preserved Tablet. My Lord does not err in His Knowledge of things nor does He forget anything.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020052","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-51.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-53.html"},{"numVerset":53,"texteArabe":"الَّذِي جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْأَرْضَ مَهْدًا وَسَلَكَ لَكُمْ فِيهَا سُبُلًا وَأَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ مَاءً فَأَخْرَجْنَا بِهِ أَزْوَاجًا مِنْ نَبَاتٍ شَتَّىٰ","tradPropre":"C'est Lui qui vous a assigné la terre comme berceau et vous y a tracé des chemins; et qui du ciel a fait descendre de l'eau avec laquelle Nous faisons germer des couples de plantes de toutes sortes.»","tradEn":"[It is He] who has made for you the earth as a bed [spread out] and inserted therein for you roadways and sent down from the sky, rain and produced thereby categories of various plants.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Parfaitement adaptée à la vie et d’une grande stabilité. Littéralement : une couche.","explicationUnanime":"Celui qui détient cette connaissance est Celui même qui a préparé la Terre de manière à ce que vous puissiez y vivre et vous y a dessiné des chemins servant à vos déplacements. Il a aussi fait descendre du Ciel l’eau de la pluie et a fait sortir de terre grâce à cette eau diverses variétés de plantes.","explicationEn":"53. My Lord is the One who made the earth spread out for you to live on and made for you on it pathways to travel on. He sent down rain water from the sky and with that water He brings forth every kind of plant.","precisionConsensus":"Tafsīr d'At-Tabarī & d'Al-Qurtubī : Allāh rappelle qu'Il a fait de la Terre un « Mahd » (un lit aplani et un berceau étendu) et y a tracé des sentiers praticables d'un bout à l'autre.","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020053","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-52.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-54.html"},{"numVerset":54,"texteArabe":"كُلُوا وَارْعَوْا أَنْعَامَكُمْ  إِنَّ فِي ذَالِكَ لَآيَاتٍ لِأُولِي النُّهَىٰ","tradPropre":"«Mangez et faites paître votre bétail». Voilà bien là des signes pour les doués d'intelligence.","tradEn":"Eat [therefrom] and pasture your livestock. Indeed in that are signs for those of intelligence.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô gens, mangez des bonnes nourritures que Nous avons créées pour vous et faites paître vos bêtes. Ces bienfaits mentionnés constituent assurément des preuves du pouvoir et de l’Unicité d’Allah adressées aux gens doués de raison.","explicationEn":"54. Eat - O people - of the pure things that I have brought forth for you, and graze your cattle. In the favours that are mentioned there are signs of Allah’s Power and Oneness for people of understanding.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020054","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-53.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-55.html"},{"numVerset":55,"texteArabe":"۞ مِنْهَا خَلَقْنَاكُمْ وَفِيهَا نُعِيدُكُمْ وَمِنْهَا نُخْرِجُكُمْ تَارَةً أُخْرَىٰ","tradPropre":"C'est d'elle (la terre) que Nous vous avons créés, et en elle Nous vous retournerons, et d'elle Nous vous ferons sortir une fois encore.","tradEn":"From it [i.e., the earth] We created you, and into it We will return you, and from it We will extract you another time.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est de la poussière de cette Terre que Nous avons créé votre père Adam et c’est d’elle que Nous vous ferons revenir lorsque vous serez enterrés après votre mort. Puis Nous vous en ferons ressortir lorsque Nous vous ressusciterons le Jour de la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"55. From the soil of the earth I created your father, Adam (peace be upon him), into it I shall return you by your being buried therein when you pass away, and from it I shall take you out you a second time when you will be resurrected on the Day of Judgment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020055","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-54.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-56.html"},{"numVerset":56,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ أَرَيْنَاهُ آيَاتِنَا كُلَّهَا فَكَذَّبَ وَأَبَىٰ","tradPropre":"Certes Nous lui avons montré tous Nos prodiges; mais il les a démentis et a refusé (de croire).","tradEn":"And We certainly showed him [i.e., Pharaoh] Our signs - all of them - but he denied and refused.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons montré à Pharaon Nos neuf signes dans leur totalité. Il en fut témoin mais il les rejeta et refusa de croire en Allah.","explicationEn":"56. I showed Pharaoh all of My nine signs. He saw them all but denied them and refused to respond by having faith in Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020056","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-55.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-57.html"},{"numVerset":57,"texteArabe":"قَالَ أَجِئْتَنَا لِتُخْرِجَنَا مِنْ أَرْضِنَا بِسِحْرِكَ يَا مُوسَىٰ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «Es-tu venu à nous, ô Moïse, pour nous faire sortir de notre terre par ta magie?","tradEn":"He said, \"Have you come to us to drive us out of our land with your magic, O Moses?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Pharaon dit: Es-tu venu nous expulser d’Egypte par la magie que tu apportes, ô Moïse, afin que tu en deviennes le souverain?","explicationEn":"57. Pharaoh said: Have you come to remove us from Egypt with the magic that you brought, O Moses, so that you can gain control over it?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020057","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-56.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-58.html"},{"numVerset":58,"texteArabe":"فَلَنَأْتِيَنَّكَ بِسِحْرٍ مِثْلِهِ فَاجْعَلْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَا نُخْلِفُهُ نَحْنُ وَلَا أَنْتَ مَكَانًا سُوًى","tradPropre":"Nous t'apporterons assurément une magie semblable. Fixe entre nous et toi un rendez-vous auquel ni nous ni toi ne manquerons, dans un lieu convenable».","tradEn":"Then we will surely bring you magic like it, so make between us and you an appointment, which we will not fail to keep and neither will you, in a place assigned.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Moïse, nous t’apporterons une magie aussi impressionnante que la tienne. Fixe-nous donc un rendez-vous sur lequel nous nous accorderons et que le lieu de notre rendez-vous soit un lieu neutre.","explicationEn":"58. We will certainly bring to, O Moses, magic similar to yours, so make an appointment between you and us at a specified time and place, which neither of us will fail to keep, and let the place be a central and even place to both groups.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020058","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-57.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-59.html"},{"numVerset":59,"texteArabe":"قَالَ مَوْعِدُكُمْ يَوْمُ الزِّينَةِ وَأَنْ يُحْشَرَ النَّاسُ ضُحًى","tradPropre":"Alors Moïse dit: «Votre rendez-vous, c'est le jour de la fête. Et que les gens se rassemblent dans la matinée».","tradEn":"[Moses] said, \"Your appointment is on the day of the festival when the people assemble at mid-morning.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Moïse dit à Pharaon: Nous nous rencontrerons à l’aube du jour où les gens se rassemblent pour célébrer leur fête.","explicationEn":"59. Moses (peace be upon him) said to Pharaoh: The appointment between you and us will be on the day of the festival when people will gather to celebrate the festival in the morning.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020059","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-58.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-60.html"},{"numVerset":60,"texteArabe":"فَتَوَلَّىٰ فِرْعَوْنُ فَجَمَعَ كَيْدَهُ ثُمَّ أَتَىٰ","tradPropre":"Pharaon, donc, se retira. Ensuite il rassembla sa ruse puis vint (au rendez-vous).","tradEn":"So Pharaoh went away, put together his plan, and then came [to Moses].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Pharaon s’éloigna alors afin de mettre au point son stratagème et sa ruse puis vint le jour du rendez-vous.","explicationEn":"60. Pharaoh went back and gathered his plots and tricks. Then he came at the specified time and place for the contest.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020060","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-59.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-61.html"},{"numVerset":61,"texteArabe":"قَالَ لَهُمْ مُوسَىٰ وَيْلَكُمْ لَا تَفْتَرُوا عَلَى اللَّهِ كَذِبًا فَيُسْحِتَكُمْ بِعَذَابٍ  وَقَدْ خَابَ مَنِ افْتَرَىٰ","tradPropre":"Moïse leur dit: «Malheur à vous! Ne forgez pas de mensonge contre Allah: sinon par un châtiment Il vous anéantira. Celui qui forge (un mensonge) est perdu».","tradEn":"Moses said to them [i.e., the magicians summoned by Pharaoh], \"Woe to you! Do not invent a lie against Allāh or He will exterminate you with a punishment; and he has failed who invents [such falsehood].\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Moïse dit aux magiciens de Pharaon en guise de conseil: Prenez garde et n’inventez pas de mensonge sur Allah en pratiquant la magie par laquelle vous trompez les gens. Il vous anéantirait alors en abattant sur vous Son châtiment. Est perdu celui qui invente des mensonges sur Allah.","explicationEn":"61. Moses said advising Pharaoh’s magicians: Beware, do not invent lies against Allah through the magic by means of which you deceive people, or He will eliminate you with a punishment from Him. Whoever invents lies against Allah is a loser.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020061","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-60.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-62.html"},{"numVerset":62,"texteArabe":"فَتَنَازَعُوا أَمْرَهُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ وَأَسَرُّوا النَّجْوَىٰ","tradPropre":"Là-dessus, ils se mirent à disputer entre eux de leur affaire et tinrent secrètes leurs discussions.","tradEn":"So they disputed over their affair among themselves and concealed their private conversation.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Suite au conseil de Moïse, les magiciens se regardèrent puis se mirent à parler à voix basse.","explicationEn":"62. The magicians argued among themselves when they heard what Moses (peace be upon him) had to say and they conferred secretly.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020062","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-61.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-63.html"},{"numVerset":63,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا إِنْ هَاذَانِ لَسَاحِرَانِ يُرِيدَانِ أَنْ يُخْرِجَاكُمْ مِنْ أَرْضِكُمْ بِسِحْرِهِمَا وَيَذْهَبَا بِطَرِيقَتِكُمُ الْمُثْلَىٰ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Voici deux magiciens qui, par leur magie, veulent vous faire abandonner votre terre et emporter votre doctrine idéale.","tradEn":"They said, \"Indeed, these are two magicians who want to drive you out of your land with their magic and do away with your most exemplary way [i.e., religion or tradition].","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Dans lequel nous sommes passés maîtres : la magie.","explicationUnanime":"Ils se dirent: Moïse et Aaron sont des magiciens qui veulent vous expulser d’Egypte grâce à leur magie et faire disparaître votre beau mode de vie et votre confession qui est la meilleure.","explicationEn":"63. The magicians said to one another secretly: Moses and Aaron are both magicians. Their intention is to drive you out of Egypt with the magic that they brought and put an end to your superior way of life and sublime religion.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020063","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-62.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-64.html"},{"numVerset":64,"texteArabe":"فَأَجْمِعُوا كَيْدَكُمْ ثُمَّ ائْتُوا صَفًّا  وَقَدْ أَفْلَحَ الْيَوْمَ مَنِ اسْتَعْلَىٰ","tradPropre":"Rassemblez donc votre ruse puis venez en rangs serrés. Et celui qui aura le dessus aujourd'hui aura réussi».","tradEn":"So resolve upon your plan and then come [forward] in line. And he has succeeded today who overcomes.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Soyez unis et ne divergez pas puis avancez en rangs et accomplissez de concert vos tours de magie. Sachez que celui qui sort vainqueur aujourd’hui remportera ce qu’il désire.","explicationEn":"64. So make a firm decision and do not differ therein. Then go forward in rows and throw down what you have all at once. Whoever defeats his opponent today has attained his objective.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020064","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-63.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-65.html"},{"numVerset":65,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا يَا مُوسَىٰ إِمَّا أَنْ تُلْقِيَ وَإِمَّا أَنْ نَكُونَ أَوَّلَ مَنْ أَلْقَىٰ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «O Moïse, ou tu jettes, [le premier ton bâton] ou que nous soyons les premiers à jeter?»","tradEn":"They said, \"O Moses, either you throw or we will be the first to throw.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les magiciens dirent à Moïse: Ô Moïse, choisis: soit c’est toi qui commence ton numéro soit c’est nous qui commençons.","explicationEn":"65. The magicians said to Moses (peace be upon him): O Moses, you have one of two options: Either you will be the first to throw down the magic you have, or we will be the first to do so.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020065","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-64.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-66.html"},{"numVerset":66,"texteArabe":"قَالَ بَلْ أَلْقُوا  فَإِذَا حِبَالُهُمْ وَعِصِيُّهُمْ يُخَيَّلُ إِلَيْهِ مِنْ سِحْرِهِمْ أَنَّهَا تَسْعَىٰ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «Jetez plutôt». Et voilà que leurs cordes et leurs bâtons lui parurent ramper par l'effet de leur magie.","tradEn":"He said, \"Rather, you throw.\" And suddenly their ropes and staffs seemed to him from their magic that they were moving [like snakes].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Moïse leur répondit: Commencez plutôt. Puis les magiciens jetèrent leurs cordes et leurs bâtons. L’effet de la magie fit apparaitre à Moïse que ces cordes et ces bâtons étaient des serpents qui se tortillaient frénétiquement.","explicationEn":"66. Moses (peace be upon him) said: Rather, you throw what you have first. So they threw what they had and suddenly their ropes and sticks that they had thrown seemed to Moses, because of their magic, to be snakes moving quickly.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020066","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-65.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-67.html"},{"numVerset":67,"texteArabe":"فَأَوْجَسَ فِي نَفْسِهِ خِيفَةً مُوسَىٰ","tradPropre":"Moïse ressentit quelque peur en lui-même.","tradEn":"And he sensed within himself apprehension, did Moses.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il dissimula la peur que lui inspira ce tour d’illusion.","explicationEn":"67. Moses was inwardly alarmed thinking that they would come for him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020067","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-66.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-68.html"},{"numVerset":68,"texteArabe":"قُلْنَا لَا تَخَفْ إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْأَعْلَىٰ","tradPropre":"Nous lui dîmes: «N'aie pas peur, c'est toi qui auras le dessus.","tradEn":"We [i.e., Allāh] said, \"Fear not. Indeed, it is you who are superior.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est alors qu’Allah lui dit afin de le rassurer: Ne sois pas apeuré par ce que tu crois voir car c’est toi, ô Moïse, qui les vaincra.","explicationEn":"68. Allah said to Moses (peace be upon him) reassuring him: Do not be afraid of what they seem to you. You - O Moses - have the upper hand over them and you will be victorious.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020068","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-67.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-69.html"},{"numVerset":69,"texteArabe":"وَأَلْقِ مَا فِي يَمِينِكَ تَلْقَفْ مَا صَنَعُوا  إِنَّمَا صَنَعُوا كَيْدُ سَاحِرٍ  وَلَا يُفْلِحُ السَّاحِرُ حَيْثُ أَتَىٰ","tradPropre":"Jette ce qu'il y a dans ta main droite; cela dévorera ce qu'ils ont fabriqué. Ce qu'ils ont fabriqué n'est qu'une ruse de magicien; et le magicien ne réussit pas, où qu'il soit».","tradEn":"And throw what is in your right hand; it will swallow up what they have crafted. What they have crafted is but the trick of a magician, and the magician will not succeed wherever he is.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Jette le bâton qui est dans ta main droite et il se muera alors en un serpent qui avalera tout le produit de leur magie. Or leur magie n’a produit qu’une illusion et son auteur ne réussit dans aucune de ses entreprises.","explicationEn":"69. Throw down the stick that is in your right hand: it will turn into a snake and swallow up the magic they have produced. They have only produced a magic trick, and a magician will not achieve his objective, wherever he may be.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020069","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-68.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-70.html"},{"numVerset":70,"texteArabe":"فَأُلْقِيَ السَّحَرَةُ سُجَّدًا قَالُوا آمَنَّا بِرَبِّ هَارُونَ وَمُوسَىٰ","tradPropre":"Les magiciens se jetèrent prosternés, disant: «Nous avons foi en le Seigneur d'Aaron et de Moïse».","tradEn":"So the magicians fell down in prostration. They said, \"We have believed in the Lord of Aaron and Moses.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Obéissant à Allah, Moïse jeta son bâton qui se transforma en un serpent et avala l’œuvre des magiciens adverses. Ces derniers se prosternèrent alors à Allah lorsqu’ils comprirent que Moïse ne pratiquait pas la magie mais apportait plutôt des signes d’Allah. Puis ils dirent: Nous croyons au Seigneur de Moïse et de Aaron, le Seigneur de toutes les créatures.","explicationEn":"70. So Moses threw down his stick and it turned into a snake and swallowed up what the magicians had produced. The magicians then all prostrated to Allah once they came to know that what Moses had was not magic, but it was from Allah and they said: We have faith in the Lord of Moses and Aaron, the Lord of all created things.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020070","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-69.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-71.html"},{"numVerset":71,"texteArabe":"قَالَ آمَنْتُمْ لَهُ قَبْلَ أَنْ آذَنَ لَكُمْ  إِنَّهُ لَكَبِيرُكُمُ الَّذِي عَلَّمَكُمُ السِّحْرَ  فَلَأُقَطِّعَنَّ أَيْدِيَكُمْ وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ مِنْ خِلَافٍ وَلَأُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ فِي جُذُوعِ النَّخْلِ وَلَتَعْلَمُنَّ أَيُّنَا أَشَدُّ عَذَابًا وَأَبْقَىٰ","tradPropre":"Alors Pharaon dit: «Avez-vous cru en lui avant que je ne vous y autorise? C'est lui votre chef qui vous a enseigné la magie. Je vous ferai sûrement, couper mains et jambes opposées, et vous ferai crucifier aux troncs des palmiers, et vous saurez, avec certitude, qui de nous est plus fort en châtiment et qui est le plus durable».","tradEn":"[Pharaoh] said, \"You believed him [i.e., Moses] before I gave you permission. Indeed, he is your leader who has taught you magic. So I will surely cut off your hands and your feet on opposite sides, and I will crucify you on the trunks of palm trees, and you will surely know which of us is more severe in [giving] punishment and more enduring.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> De moi ou du Seigneur de Moïse.","explicationUnanime":"Pharaon, réprouvant le comportement des magiciens et leur conversion à la foi, leur dit sur un ton menaçant: Avez-vous cru en Moïse avant que je ne vous l’autorise? Il doit être votre chef qui vous a appris vos tours de magie. Je vous punirai en amputant chacun de vous un pied et une main des côtés opposés et je vous crucifierai aux troncs des palmiers jusqu’à ce que mort s’ensuive. Vous servirez ainsi d’exemple à d’autres et vous saurez qui de moi ou du Seigneur de Moïse châtie le plus sévèrement.","explicationEn":"71. Pharaoh said in rejection of the faith of the magicians and as threat to them: Have you believed in Moses before I have given you permission to do so? Moses must be your master - O magicians - who taught you magic. I shall certainly cut off from each one of you one hand and foot from opposite sides, then I will crucify your bodies on the trunks of palm trees until you die. You will become a lesson for others and you will know then which of us has the fiercer and more lasting punishment: I or the Lord of Moses?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020071","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-70.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-72.html"},{"numVerset":72,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا لَنْ نُؤْثِرَكَ عَلَىٰ مَا جَاءَنَا مِنَ الْبَيِّنَاتِ وَالَّذِي فَطَرَنَا  فَاقْضِ مَا أَنْتَ قَاضٍ  إِنَّمَا تَقْضِي هَاذِهِ الْحَيَاةَ الدُّنْيَا","tradPropre":"«Par celui qui nous a créés, dirent-ils, nous ne te préférerons jamais à ce qui nous est parvenu comme preuves évidentes. Décrète donc ce que tu as à décréter. Tes décrets ne touchent que cette présente vie.","tradEn":"They said, \"Never will we prefer you over what has come to us of clear proofs and [over] He who created us. So decree whatever you are to decree. You can only decree for this worldly life.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les magiciens rétorquèrent à Pharaon: Ô Pharaon, nous ne préférerons pas te suivre et faire fi des signes clairs qui nous sont parvenus. Nous ne te préfèrerons pas à Allah qui nous a créés. Prononce donc contre nous la sentence que tu veux car ton autorité sur nous ne se limite qu’à ce bas monde éphémère et prendra fin tôt ou tard.","explicationEn":"72. The magicians said to Pharaoh: We shall never prefer following you - O Pharaoh - to following the clear signs that have come to us. We will never prefer you to Allah Who created us. So do whatever you want to us: you only have power over us in this present transient life, and your power will soon vanish.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020072","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-71.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-73.html"},{"numVerset":73,"texteArabe":"إِنَّا آمَنَّا بِرَبِّنَا لِيَغْفِرَ لَنَا خَطَايَانَا وَمَا أَكْرَهْتَنَا عَلَيْهِ مِنَ السِّحْرِ  وَاللَّهُ خَيْرٌ وَأَبْقَىٰ","tradPropre":"Nous croyons en notre Seigneur, afin qu'Il nous pardonne nos fautes ainsi que la magie à laquelle tu nous as contraints». Et Allah est meilleur et éternel.","tradEn":"Indeed, we have believed in our Lord that He may forgive us our sins and what you compelled us [to do] of magic. And Allāh is better and more enduring.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ou : le châtiment d’Allah est plus terrible et plus durable.","explicationUnanime":"Nous croyons en notre Seigneur afin que, peut-être, il efface notre mécréance et nos péchés passés, dont fait partie la magie que tu nous as contraints de pratiquer et de nous en servir au détriment de Moïse. Allah détient une rétribution meilleure que celle que tu nous as promise et son châtiment est plus durable que celui dont tu nous menaces.","explicationEn":"73. We believe in our Lord, with the hope that He will erase from us our past sins of disbelief and other sins, and that He will erase from us the sin of magic that you forced us to learn, practice and challenge Moses with. Allah has a better reward than what you promise us and His punishment is more lasting than the punishment you threaten us with.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020073","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-72.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-74.html"},{"numVerset":74,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهُ مَنْ يَأْتِ رَبَّهُ مُجْرِمًا فَإِنَّ لَهُ جَهَنَّمَ لَا يَمُوتُ فِيهَا وَلَا يَحْيَىٰ","tradPropre":"Quiconque vient en criminel à son Seigneur, aura certes l'Enfer où il ne meurt ni ne vit.","tradEn":"Indeed, whoever comes to his Lord as a criminal - indeed, for him is Hell; he will neither die therein nor live.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"En conclusion, celui qui se présente à son Seigneur le Jour de la Résurrection alors qu’il a mécru en Lui dans le bas monde ira en Enfer et y demeurera éternellement. Il n’y connaîtra ni la mort salvatrice ni n’y vivra une vie agréable.","explicationEn":"74. The matter and gist is that those who come to their Lord on the Day of Judgment as disbelievers will enter the fire to remain there forever. Therein they will not die and be relieved of its torment, nor will they live a pleasant life.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020074","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-73.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-75.html"},{"numVerset":75,"texteArabe":"وَمَنْ يَأْتِهِ مُؤْمِنًا قَدْ عَمِلَ الصَّالِحَاتِ فَأُولَائِكَ لَهُمُ الدَّرَجَاتُ الْعُلَىٰ","tradPropre":"Et quiconque vient auprès de Lui en croyant, après avoir fait de bonnes œuvres, voilà donc ceux qui auront les plus hauts rangs,","tradEn":"But whoever comes to Him as a believer having done righteous deeds - for those will be the highest degrees [in position]:","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Quant à celui qui se présentera à son Seigneur le Jour de la Résurrection en ayant cru en Lui dans le bas monde et en ayant accompli de bonnes œuvres, il aura un rang élevé et occupera des degrés supérieurs.","explicationEn":"75. Those who come to their Sustainer on the Day of Judgement as believers who had done righteous actions, then such people will be rewarded with lofty abodes and high ranks in Paradise.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020075","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-74.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-76.html"},{"numVerset":76,"texteArabe":"جَنَّاتُ عَدْنٍ تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْأَنْهَارُ خَالِدِينَ فِيهَا  وَذَالِكَ جَزَاءُ مَنْ تَزَكَّىٰ","tradPropre":"les jardins du séjour (éternel), sous lesquels coulent les ruisseaux, où ils demeureront éternellement. Et voilà la récompense de ceux qui se purifient [de la mécréance et des péchés].","tradEn":"Gardens of perpetual residence beneath which rivers flow, wherein they abide eternally. And that is the reward of one who purifies himself.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces degrés supérieurs consisteront en des vergers et des rivières coulant sous leurs palais, et il y séjournera éternellement. Cette rétribution sera celle de tous ceux qui renoncent à la mécréance et aux actes de désobéissance.","explicationEn":"76. Those ranks are Gardens of Eternity with streams flowing under their palaces, and there they will stay there forever. That is the reward of those who purify themselves from disbelief and sins.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020076","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-75.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-77.html"},{"numVerset":77,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَىٰ مُوسَىٰ أَنْ أَسْرِ بِعِبَادِي فَاضْرِبْ لَهُمْ طَرِيقًا فِي الْبَحْرِ يَبَسًا لَا تَخَافُ دَرَكًا وَلَا تَخْشَىٰ","tradPropre":"Nous révélâmes à Moïse: «Pars la nuit, à la tête de Mes serviteurs, puis, trace-leur un passage à sec dans la mer: sans craindre une poursuite et sans éprouver aucune peur».","tradEn":"And We had inspired to Moses, \"Travel by night with My servants and strike for them a dry path through the sea; you will not fear being overtaken [by Pharaoh] nor be afraid [of drowning].\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons révélé à Moïse de sortir Mes serviteurs d’Egypte de nuit afin que personne ne s’en rende compte et de frapper l’eau de la mer à l’aide de son bâton afin de leur frayer un passage sûr et à sec. Nous lui avons aussi révélé de ne pas craindre que Pharaon et ses notables le suivent et de pas craindre d’être noyé.","explicationEn":"77. And I revealed to Moses to take My servants by night from Egypt so that nobody notices them, and make for them a dry path in the sea after striking the sea with the staff, safely without fearing Pharaoh and his people catching up with you nor being scared of drowning in the sea.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020077","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-76.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-78.html"},{"numVerset":78,"texteArabe":"فَأَتْبَعَهُمْ فِرْعَوْنُ بِجُنُودِهِ فَغَشِيَهُمْ مِنَ الْيَمِّ مَا غَشِيَهُمْ","tradPropre":"Pharaon les poursuivit avec ses armées. La mer les submergea bel et bien.","tradEn":"So Pharaoh pursued them with his soldiers, and there covered them from the sea that which covered them,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Pharaon accompagné de ses soldats les poursuivirent mais ils furent tous submergés par des trombes d’eau dont Allah seul connaît l’immensité. Ils se noyèrent ainsi tous et moururent tandis que Moïse et ceux qui l’accompagnaient furent sauvés.","explicationEn":"78. Then Pharoah, accompanied by his armies, followed them. Then he and his armies were engulfed by part of the sea, the reality of which only Allah knows. They all drowned and perished, whilst Moses and those with him were saved.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020078","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-77.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-79.html"},{"numVerset":79,"texteArabe":"وَأَضَلَّ فِرْعَوْنُ قَوْمَهُ وَمَا هَدَىٰ","tradPropre":"Pharaon égara ainsi son peuple et ne le mît pas sur le droit chemin.","tradEn":"And Pharaoh led his people astray and did not guide [them].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Pharaon a assurément égaré son peuple en lui imposant la mécréance qu’il leur a embellie et le faux par lequel il les a trompés et il ne les a certainement pas orientés vers le chemin de la guidée.","explicationEn":"79. And Pharaoh misguided his people by making disbelief appear good to them and by deceiving them through falsehood, and he did not direct them towards the path of guidance.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020079","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-78.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-80.html"},{"numVerset":80,"texteArabe":"يَا بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ قَدْ أَنْجَيْنَاكُمْ مِنْ عَدُوِّكُمْ وَوَاعَدْنَاكُمْ جَانِبَ الطُّورِ الْأَيْمَنَ وَنَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوَىٰ","tradPropre":"O Enfants d'Israël, Nous vous avons déjà délivrés de votre ennemi, et Nous vous avons donné rendez-vous sur le flanc droit du Mont. Et Nous avons fait descendre sur vous la manne et les cailles.","tradEn":"O Children of Israel, We delivered you from your enemy, and We made an appointment with you at the right side of the mount, and We sent down to you manna and quails,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Après les avoir sauvés de Pharaon et de ses soldats, Nous dîmes aux Israélites: Ô enfants d’Israël, Nous vous avons sauvés de votre ennemi et Nous avons promis de parler à Moïse sur le versant droit de la vallée située à côté du mont Aṭ-Ṭûr. Nous avons de plus fait descendre sur vous, durant votre errance dans le désert, certains de Nos bienfaits, dont une boisson aussi sucrée que le miel et un petit oiseau à la viande succulent ressemblant à la caille.","explicationEn":"80. And I said to the Children of Israel after saving them from Pharoah and his armies: “O Children of Israel, I saved you from your enemy, and I promised you that I will speak to Moses to the right of the valley by Mount Tur, and I sent down to you whilst you were wandering food you can eat which is sweet and resembles gum, and birds which resemble quails.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020080","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-79.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-81.html"},{"numVerset":81,"texteArabe":"كُلُوا مِنْ طَيِّبَاتِ مَا رَزَقْنَاكُمْ وَلَا تَطْغَوْا فِيهِ فَيَحِلَّ عَلَيْكُمْ غَضَبِي  وَمَنْ يَحْلِلْ عَلَيْهِ غَضَبِي فَقَدْ هَوَىٰ","tradPropre":"«Mangez des bonnes choses que Nous vous avons attribuées et ne vous montrez pas ingrats, sinon Ma colère s'abattra sur vous: et celui sur qui Ma colère s'abat, va sûrement vers l'abîme.","tradEn":"[Saying], \"Eat from the good things with which We have provided you and do not transgress [or oppress others] therein, lest My anger should descend upon you. And he upon whom My anger descends has certainly fallen [i.e., perished].\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Mangez des nourritures succulentes et licites dont Nous vous avons fait don et n’approchez pas ce que Nous vous avons rendu illicite car Ma colère s’abattrait sur vous. Or ceux qui encourent ma colère sont anéantis et connaissent le malheur dans ce bas monde et dans l’au-delà.","explicationEn":"81. Eat the wholesome lawful foods I have provided you and do not go beyond what I have made lawful to you, so you consume what I have made forbidden for you, otherwise My anger will fall on you. Whoever My anger falls upon will be destroyed and fall into Hell.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020081","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-80.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-82.html"},{"numVerset":82,"texteArabe":"وَإِنِّي لَغَفَّارٌ لِمَنْ تَابَ وَآمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا ثُمَّ اهْتَدَىٰ","tradPropre":"Et je suis Grand Pardonneur à celui qui se repent, croit, fait bonne œuvre, puis se met sur le bon chemin».","tradEn":"But indeed, I am the Perpetual Forgiver of whoever repents and believes and does righteousness and then continues in guidance.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Cependant, Je pardonne et absous généreusement ceux qui se repentent à Moi, croient en Moi, accomplissent de bonnes œuvres puis restent fidèles à la vérité","explicationEn":"82. And I am extremely forgiving and pardoning to one who repents to Me, does good deeds and is then firm on the truth.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020082","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-81.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-83.html"},{"numVerset":83,"texteArabe":"۞ وَمَا أَعْجَلَكَ عَنْ قَوْمِكَ يَا مُوسَىٰ","tradPropre":"«Pourquoi Moïse t'es-tu hâté de quitter ton peuple?»","tradEn":"[Allāh said], \"And what made you hasten from your people, O Moses?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Moïse, quelle est la raison qui t’a fait prématurément quitter les tiens et marcher devant eux sans désigner personne à leur tête pour te remplacer?","explicationEn":"83. And what has made you rush from your people, O Moses, leaving them behind?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020083","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-82.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-84.html"},{"numVerset":84,"texteArabe":"قَالَ هُمْ أُولَاءِ عَلَىٰ أَثَرِي وَعَجِلْتُ إِلَيْكَ رَبِّ لِتَرْضَىٰ","tradPropre":"Ils sont là sur mes traces, dit Moïse. Et je me suis hâté vers Toi, Seigneur, afin que Tu sois satisfait.","tradEn":"He said, \"They are close upon my tracks, and I hastened to You, my Lord, that You be pleased.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Moïse répondit: Ils ne sont pas loin derrière moi et sont sur le point de me rattraper. Je ne me suis mis à marcher devant eux et empressé de venir à Ta rencontre que pour obtenir Ton agrément.","explicationEn":"84. Moses (peace be upon him) said: “Here they are behind me. They shall catch up with me. I preceded my people in coming to You, so that you become pleased with me for coming towards You quickly”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020084","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-83.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-85.html"},{"numVerset":85,"texteArabe":"قَالَ فَإِنَّا قَدْ فَتَنَّا قَوْمَكَ مِنْ بَعْدِكَ وَأَضَلَّهُمُ السَّامِرِيُّ","tradPropre":"Allah dit: «Nous avons mis ton peuple à l'épreuve après ton départ. Et le Sâmirî les a égarés».","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"But indeed, We have tried your people after you [departed], and the Sāmirī has led them astray.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> En l’incitant à adorer le Veau d’or.","explicationUnanime":"Allah lui dit: Sache que Nous avons éprouvé le peuple que tu as laissé derrière toi par un Veau que le Samaritain les a invités à adorer et ce dernier les égara.","explicationEn":"85. Allah said: “I have tested your people whom you left behind through worship of the calf. Samiri called them to worshipping it and he has misguided them through this”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020085","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-84.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-86.html"},{"numVerset":86,"texteArabe":"فَرَجَعَ مُوسَىٰ إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِ غَضْبَانَ أَسِفًا  قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ أَلَمْ يَعِدْكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ وَعْدًا حَسَنًا  أَفَطَالَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْعَهْدُ أَمْ أَرَدْتُمْ أَنْ يَحِلَّ عَلَيْكُمْ غَضَبٌ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ فَأَخْلَفْتُمْ مَوْعِدِي","tradPropre":"Moïse retourna donc vers son peuple, courroucé et chagriné; il dit: «O mon peuple, votre Seigneur ne vous a-t-Il pas déjà fait une belle promesse? L'alliance a-t-elle donc été trop longue pour vous? ou avez-vous désiré que la colère de votre Seigneur s'abatte sur vous, pour avoir trahi votre engagement envers moi?»","tradEn":"So Moses returned to his people, angry and grieved. He said, \"O my people, did your Lord not make you a good promise? Then, was the time [of its fulfillment] too long for you, or did you wish that wrath from your Lord descend upon you, so you broke your promise [of obedience] to me?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Moïse retourna alors auprès des siens, plein de colère et de tristesse pour eux. Arrivés auprès d’eux, il leur dit: Ô mon peuple, Allah ne vous a-t-il pas fait la promesse agréable de vous révéler la Torah et de vous faire entrer au Paradis? Le temps qui s’est écoulé depuis a-t-il été long au point que vous ayez oublié ou voulez-vous que la colère et le châtiment de votre Seigneur s’abattent sur vous à cause d’un tel comportement? Est-ce pour cela que vous avez manqué à votre promesse de rester obéissants à Allah jusqu’à mon retour?","explicationEn":"86. Moses returned to his people, angered by their worship of the calf and grieving over them. Moses (peace be upon him) said: “My people, did Allah not make you a good promise that He will send the Torah to you and enter you into paradise? Had a long time passed upon you that you forgot? Or did you intend through this action of yours that your Lord’s anger should descend upon you and His punishment befall you, and this is why you broke your promise to me to stay firm on obedience until I return to you?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020086","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-85.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-87.html"},{"numVerset":87,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا مَا أَخْلَفْنَا مَوْعِدَكَ بِمَلْكِنَا وَلَاكِنَّا حُمِّلْنَا أَوْزَارًا مِنْ زِينَةِ الْقَوْمِ فَقَذَفْنَاهَا فَكَذَالِكَ أَلْقَى السَّامِرِيُّ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Ce n'est pas de notre propre gré que nous avons manqué à notre engagement envers toi. Mais nous fûmes chargés de fardeaux d'ornements du peuple (de Pharaon); nous les avons donc jetés (sur le feu) tout comme le Sâmirî les a lancés.","tradEn":"They said, \"We did not break our promise to you by our will, but we were made to carry burdens from the ornaments of the people [of Pharaoh], so we threw them [into the fire], and thus did the Sāmirī throw.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les compatriotes de Moïse répondirent: Ô Moïse, nous n’avons pas manqué délibérément à cette promesse. Nous y avons plutôt été contraints. En effet, nous avons rassemblé quantité de bijoux appartenant aux gens de Pharaon et les avons jetés dans un trou afin de nous en défaire mais le Samaritain jeta par-dessus de la terre provenant du sabot de la jument de Gabriel.","explicationEn":"87. Moses’ people said: “We did not break your promise, O Moses, by our own choice, but rather by compulsion. We carried large weights of the jewellery of Pharaoh’s people and we threw them into a ditch to get rid of them. But as we threw them into the ditch, Samiri threw into it some dust he had from the hoof of the horse of Gabriel (peace be upon him)”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020087","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-86.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-88.html"},{"numVerset":88,"texteArabe":"فَأَخْرَجَ لَهُمْ عِجْلًا جَسَدًا لَهُ خُوَارٌ فَقَالُوا هَاذَا إِلَاهُكُمْ وَإِلَاهُ مُوسَىٰ فَنَسِيَ","tradPropre":"Puis il en a fait sortir pour eux un veau, un corps à mugissement. Et ils ont dit: «C'est votre divinité et la divinité de Moïse; il a donc oublié»!","tradEn":"And he extracted for them [the statue of] a calf which had a lowing sound, and they said, \"This is your god and the god of Moses, but he forgot.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> A partir des bijoux ainsi fondus.<br><br><strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Le son était en réalité produit par le vent léger qui s’y engouffrait (Voir Tafsîr ibn Kathîr).","explicationUnanime":"Ensuite, le Samaritain a façonné grâce à ces bijoux le corps sans vie d’un veau… qui mugissait comme un vrai veau, et le présenta aux Israélites. Ceux qui ont été charmés par l’œuvre du Samaritain dirent: Ceci est votre dieu adoré et le dieu de Moïse mais celui-ci l’a oublié et l’a laissé ici.","explicationEn":"88. So Samiri took out from this jewellery of the Israelites a lifeless body of a calf, which made a noise like that of a cow. Those amongst them who had been tempted by Samiri’s action said: “This is your god and the god of Moses which he forgot and left here”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020088","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-87.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-89.html"},{"numVerset":89,"texteArabe":"أَفَلَا يَرَوْنَ أَلَّا يَرْجِعُ إِلَيْهِمْ قَوْلًا وَلَا يَمْلِكُ لَهُمْ ضَرًّا وَلَا نَفْعًا","tradPropre":"Quoi! Ne voyaient-ils pas qu'il [le veau] ne leur rendait aucune parole et qu'il ne possédait aucun moyen de leur nuire ou de leur faire du bien?","tradEn":"Did they not see that it could not return to them any speech [i.e., response] and that it did not possess for them any harm or benefit?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces gens qui ont été tentés par le Veau et l’ont adoré ne voyaient-ils pas qu’il ne leur parlait pas, ne leur répondait pas, n’éloignait pas d'eux, ni de quiconque d’autre, le mal et ne leur procurait aucun bien à eux ni à personne?","explicationEn":"89. Do these people who were tempted by the calf and then worshipped it not see that the calf does not speak or respond to them, nor does it have the ability to remove harm from them or others or bring benefit for itself or others?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020089","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-88.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-90.html"},{"numVerset":90,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ قَالَ لَهُمْ هَارُونُ مِنْ قَبْلُ يَا قَوْمِ إِنَّمَا فُتِنْتُمْ بِهِ  وَإِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ الرَّحْمَانُ فَاتَّبِعُونِي وَأَطِيعُوا أَمْرِي","tradPropre":"Certes, Aaron leur avait bien dit auparavant: «O mon peuple, vous êtes tombés dans la tentation (à cause du veau). Or, c'est le Tout Miséricordieux qui est vraiment votre Seigneur. Suivez-moi donc et obéissez à mon commandement».","tradEn":"And Aaron had already told them before [the return of Moses], \"O my people, you are only being tested by it, and indeed, your Lord is the Most Merciful, so follow me and obey my order.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Aaron leur avait pourtant bien dit avant le retour de Moïse: Le façonnement de ce veau à partir de bijoux et le fait qu’il émette des mugissements ne font partie que d’un test qui distinguera parmi vous les croyants des mécréants. Ô gens, c’est votre Seigneur qui détient le pouvoir de vous faire miséricorde et non celui qui n’a ni le pouvoir d’être utile ni le pouvoir d’être nuisible, et donc, à plus forte raison, ne peut en aucun cas vous faire miséricorde.","explicationEn":"90. Aaron had said to them before Moses returned to them: “The making of the calf from gold and its mooing are only to test you, to distinguish the believer from the disbeliever. And your Lord, O people, is Allah, so follow me by worshipping Him alone and obey my command to leave worshipping others besides Him”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020090","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-89.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-91.html"},{"numVerset":91,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا لَنْ نَبْرَحَ عَلَيْهِ عَاكِفِينَ حَتَّىٰ يَرْجِعَ إِلَيْنَا مُوسَىٰ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Nous continuerons à y être attachés, jusqu'à ce que Moïse retourne vers nous».","tradEn":"They said, \"We will never cease being devoted to it [i.e., the calf] until Moses returns to us.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceux qui ont été tentés par l’adoration du Veau dirent: Nous ne cesserons de l’adorer jusqu’à ce que Moïse revienne auprès de nous.","explicationEn":"91. Those who had been tempted through worship of the calf said: “We will continue worshipping it until Moses returns to us”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020091","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-90.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-92.html"},{"numVerset":92,"texteArabe":"قَالَ يَا هَارُونُ مَا مَنَعَكَ إِذْ رَأَيْتَهُمْ ضَلُّوا","tradPropre":"Alors [Moïse] dit: «Qu'est-ce qui t'a empêché, Aaron, quand tu les as vus s'égarer,","tradEn":"[Moses] said, \"O Aaron, what prevented you, when you saw them going astray,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Après son retour, Moïse dit à son frère: Quelle raison t’a empêchée, lorsque tu les as vus s’égarer en adorant le Veau au lieu d’Allah.","explicationEn":"92. Moses said to his brother Aaron: “What was it that stopped you, when you saw them go astray by worshipping the calf besides Allah,","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020092","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-91.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-93.html"},{"numVerset":93,"texteArabe":"أَلَّا تَتَّبِعَنِ  أَفَعَصَيْتَ أَمْرِي","tradPropre":"de me suivre? As-tu donc désobéi à mon commandement?»","tradEn":"From following me? Then have you disobeyed my order?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"de les délaisser et de me rattraper? As-tu donc désobéi à mon ordre de me remplacer à leur tête?","explicationEn":"93. from leaving them and joining me? Did you disobey my order to you when I made you my deputy over them?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020093","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-92.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-94.html"},{"numVerset":94,"texteArabe":"قَالَ يَا ابْنَ أُمَّ لَا تَأْخُذْ بِلِحْيَتِي وَلَا بِرَأْسِي  إِنِّي خَشِيتُ أَنْ تَقُولَ فَرَّقْتَ بَيْنَ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ وَلَمْ تَرْقُبْ قَوْلِي","tradPropre":"[Aaron] dit: «O fils de ma mère, ne me prends ni par la barbe ni par la tête. Je craignais que tu ne dises: «Tu as divisé les enfants d'Israël et tu n'as pas observé mes ordres».","tradEn":"[Aaron] said, \"O son of my mother, do not seize [me] by my beard or by my head. Indeed, I feared that you would say, 'You caused division among the Children of Israel, and you did not observe [or await] my word.'\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est alors que Moïse empoigna la barbe et la tête de son frère et le tira vers lui en signe de réprobation. Aaron protesta en ces termes afin de le calmer: Ne me saisis ni par la barbe ni par les cheveux car je suis resté parmi eux pour une excuse valable: j’ai en effet craint que si je les laisse livrés à eux-mêmes, ils ne se divisent. Tu m’aurais alors reproché cette division et d’avoir manqué à la promesse que je t’avais faite.","explicationEn":"94. When Moses took his brother by his beard and head, dragging him and scolding him for what he did, Aaron said to him, seeking his compassion: “Do not hold my beard and the hair on my head, for I have a reason for staying with them. I feared if I leave them alone they will disperse, then you will say I split them apart and that I did not maintain your bequest regarding them”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020094","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-93.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-95.html"},{"numVerset":95,"texteArabe":"قَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكَ يَا سَامِرِيُّ","tradPropre":"Alors [Moïse] dit: «Quel a été ton dessein? O Sâmirî?»","tradEn":"[Moses] said, \"And what is your case, O Sāmirī?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis Moïse dit au Samaritain: Pourquoi avoir agi ainsi?","explicationEn":"95. Moses (peace be upon him) said to Samiri: “What is your matter, O Samiri? What made you do what you did?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020095","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-94.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-96.html"},{"numVerset":96,"texteArabe":"قَالَ بَصُرْتُ بِمَا لَمْ يَبْصُرُوا بِهِ فَقَبَضْتُ قَبْضَةً مِنْ أَثَرِ الرَّسُولِ فَنَبَذْتُهَا وَكَذَالِكَ سَوَّلَتْ لِي نَفْسِي","tradPropre":"Il dit: «J'ai vu ce qu'ils n'ont pas vu: j'ai donc pris une poignée de la trace de l'Envoyé; puis, je l'ai lancée. Voilà ce que mon âme m'a suggéré».","tradEn":"He said, \"I saw what they did not see, so I took a handful [of dust] from the track of the messenger and threw it, and thus did my soul entice me.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> L’ange Gabriel, selon la majorité des exégètes.","explicationUnanime":"Il répondit: Je voyais ce qu’ils ne voyaient pas puisque j’ai vu Gabriel sur sa jument et j’ai prélevé une poignée de terre de la trace laissée par les sabots de la jument puis l’ai jetée sur les bijoux qui ont été fondus afin d’en façonner la forme d’un veau. C’est alors que le corps mugissant d’un veau prit forme et c’est ce résultat que mon âme m’a embelli.","explicationEn":"96. Samiri said to Moses (peace be upon him): “I saw what they did not see: I saw Gabriel on a horse, so I took a handful of soil from the footsteps of his horse and threw it on melted jewellery which was moulded into the form of a calf. From this, the body of a calf with a mooing sound was formed. And this is how my soul made what I did appealing to me”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020096","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-95.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-97.html"},{"numVerset":97,"texteArabe":"قَالَ فَاذْهَبْ فَإِنَّ لَكَ فِي الْحَيَاةِ أَنْ تَقُولَ لَا مِسَاسَ  وَإِنَّ لَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَنْ تُخْلَفَهُ  وَانْظُرْ إِلَىٰ إِلَاهِكَ الَّذِي ظَلْتَ عَلَيْهِ عَاكِفًا  لَنُحَرِّقَنَّهُ ثُمَّ لَنَنْسِفَنَّهُ فِي الْيَمِّ نَسْفًا","tradPropre":"«Va-t-en, dit [Moïse]. Dans la vie, tu auras à dire (à tout le monde): «Ne me touchez pas!» Et il y aura pour toi un rendez-vous que tu ne pourras manquer. Regarde ta divinité que tu as adorée avec assiduité. Nous la brûlerons certes, et ensuite, nous disperserons [sa cendre] dans les flots.","tradEn":"[Moses] said, \"Then go. And indeed, it is [decreed] for you in [this] life to say, 'No contact.' And indeed, you have an appointment [in the Hereafter] you will not fail to keep. And look at your 'god' to which you remained devoted. We will surely burn it and blow it [i.e., its ashes] into the sea with a blast.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Moïse dit au Samaritain: Pars donc. Ta punition sera que tu dises ta vie durant « Je ne toucherai personne et personne ne me touchera ». Tu vivras ainsi rejeté et de surcroît, il t’est fixé un rendez-vous le Jour de la Résurrection, afin que tu rendes des comptes et que tu sois puni et Allah ne manquera pas ce rendez-vous. Regarde maintenant le veau que tu as pris comme divinité et que tu adorais à la place d’Allah: nous le brûlerons jusqu’à ce qu’il fonde dans sa totalité puis nous disperserons ses restes dans la mer jusqu’à ce qu’il n’en reste aucune trace.","explicationEn":"97. Moses (peace be upon him) said to Samiri: “Go, for it is written for you that you will say as long as you live: ‘I am not to touch or be touched’. You will live as an outcast, and you have a promised time on the Day of Judgment in which you will be reckoned and punished. Allah will never break this promise with you. And look towards your calf which you had made your god and which you continued to worship besides Allah. We shall burn it in a fire until it melts, then we shall scatter it into the sea until no trace of it remains.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020097","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-96.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-98.html"},{"numVerset":98,"texteArabe":"إِنَّمَا إِلَاهُكُمُ اللَّهُ الَّذِي لَا إِلَاهَ إِلَّا هُوَ  وَسِعَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ عِلْمًا","tradPropre":"En vérité, votre seul Dieu est Allah en dehors de qui il n'y a point de divinité. De Sa science Il embrasse tout.","tradEn":"Your god is only Allāh, except for whom there is no deity. He has encompassed all things in knowledge.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô gens, le seul Dieu méritant d’être adoré est Allah et aucune autre divinité. Il enveloppe tout de Sa connaissance et rien ne Lui échappe.","explicationEn":"98. Your true god, O people, is Allah only, besides whom there is no true god. He has encompassed everything in His knowledge; only He knows everything and nothing escapes His awareness”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020098","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-97.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-99.html"},{"numVerset":99,"texteArabe":"كَذَالِكَ نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ أَنْبَاءِ مَا قَدْ سَبَقَ  وَقَدْ آتَيْنَاكَ مِنْ لَدُنَّا ذِكْرًا","tradPropre":"C'est ainsi que Nous te racontons les récits de ce qui s'est passé. C'est bien un rappel de Notre part que Nous t'avons apporté.","tradEn":"Thus, [O Muḥammad], We relate to you from the news of what has preceded. And We have certainly given you from Us a message [i.e., the Qur’ān].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, tout comme Nous t’avons raconté le récit de Moïse, Pharaon et leurs peuples respectifs, Nous te racontons les récits des prophètes et des peuples qui t’ont précédé afin de te consoler. Nous t’avons de plus, donné le Coran qui sert de rappel à ceux qui veulent se rappeler.","explicationEn":"99. Just as I related to you, O Messenger, the story of Moses, Pharaoh and their people, I relate to you the incidents of the prophets and nations before you, so that they are a solace for you. And I have given you from Myself a Qur’ān through which those who seek reminders are reminded.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020099","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-98.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-100.html"},{"numVerset":100,"texteArabe":"مَنْ أَعْرَضَ عَنْهُ فَإِنَّهُ يَحْمِلُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وِزْرًا","tradPropre":"Quiconque s'en détourne (de ce Coran), portera au jour de la résurrection un fardeau;","tradEn":"Whoever turns away from it - then indeed, he will bear on the Day of Resurrection a burden [i.e., great sin],","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Celui qui se détourne de ce Coran qui t’a été révélé et n’y croit pas, se présentera le Jour de la Résurrection coupable d’un péché grave qui lui vaudra d’être châtié douloureusement.","explicationEn":"100. Whoever turns away from this Qur’ān which has been revealed to you and does not believe in it and act accordingly will come on the Day of Judgment carrying great sin and deserving a painful punishment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020100","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-99.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-101.html"},{"numVerset":101,"texteArabe":"خَالِدِينَ فِيهِ  وَسَاءَ لَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ حِمْلًا","tradPropre":"ils resteront éternellement dans cet état, et quel mauvais fardeau pour eux au Jour de la Résurrection,","tradEn":"[Abiding] eternally therein, and evil it is for them on the Day of Resurrection as a load -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"De tels gens subiront ce châtiment pour l’éternité et comme est mauvaise, cette charge qu’est ce grave péché, qu’ils porteront le jour de la Résurrection","explicationEn":"101. Staying in this punishment forever. How awful a burden they will be carrying on the day of judgment.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020101","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-100.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-102.html"},{"numVerset":102,"texteArabe":"يَوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِي الصُّورِ  وَنَحْشُرُ الْمُجْرِمِينَ يَوْمَئِذٍ زُرْقًا","tradPropre":"Le jour où l'on soufflera dans la Trompe, ce jour-là Nous rassemblerons les criminels tout bleus (de peur)!","tradEn":"The Day the Horn will be blown. And We will gather the criminals, that Day, blue-eyed.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ou : aveugles. Ou encore : assoiffés.","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque le deuxième souffle dans la Trompe effectué par l’ange annoncera la Ressuscitation, Nous rassemblerons ce jour-là les mécréants et ces derniers deviendront bleus tellement ils seront impressionnés par ce qu’ils verront de terrifiant dans l’au-delà.","explicationEn":"102. The day when the angel will blow in the trumpet a second time for the resurrection, and I shall gather the disbelievers on this day, blue-eyed, due to their complexion and eyes changing out of the severe horrors of the afterlife they will face.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020102","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-101.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-103.html"},{"numVerset":103,"texteArabe":"يَتَخَافَتُونَ بَيْنَهُمْ إِنْ لَبِثْتُمْ إِلَّا عَشْرًا","tradPropre":"Ils chuchoteront entre eux: «Vous n'êtes restés là que dix [jours]!»","tradEn":"They will murmur among themselves, \"You remained not but ten [days in the world].\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils se chuchoteront les uns aux autres: Vous êtes restés dans le monde intermédiaire dix jours seulement.","explicationEn":"103. They will talk to one another quietly saying: “You did not stay in the Transitory Stage after death except ten nights”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020103","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-102.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-104.html"},{"numVerset":104,"texteArabe":"نَحْنُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَقُولُونَ إِذْ يَقُولُ أَمْثَلُهُمْ طَرِيقَةً إِنْ لَبِثْتُمْ إِلَّا يَوْمًا","tradPropre":"Nous connaissons parfaitement ce qu'ils diront lorsque l'un d'entre eux dont la conduite est exemplaire dira: «Vous n'êtes restés qu'un jour».","tradEn":"We are most knowing of what they say when the best of them in manner [i.e., wisdom or speech] will say, \"You remained not but one day.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous sommes le mieux au fait de ce qu’ils se diront en secret et rien ne Nous en échappera, particulièrement lorsque le plus raisonnable parmi eux dira: Vous n’êtes restés dans le monde intermédiaire qu’un seul jour.","explicationEn":"104. I know best what they secretly say amongst themselves, with none of it escaping Me, when the most intelligent of them says: “You did not stay in the Transitory Stage except for one day, no more”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020104","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-103.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-105.html"},{"numVerset":105,"texteArabe":"وَيَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الْجِبَالِ فَقُلْ يَنْسِفُهَا رَبِّي نَسْفًا","tradPropre":"Et ils t'interrogent au sujet des montagnes. Dis: «Mon Seigneur les dispersera comme la poussière,","tradEn":"And they ask you about the mountains, so say, \"My Lord will blow them away with a blast.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, les mécréants t’interrogent au sujet de ce qu’il adviendra des montagnes le Jour de la Résurrection. Réponds-leur: Allah les déracinera et les pulvérisera.","explicationEn":"105. They ask you, O Messenger, regarding the condition of the mountains on the Day of Judgment. Say to them: My Lord will pull out the mountains from their roots and scatter them, then they will become dust.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020105","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-104.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-106.html"},{"numVerset":106,"texteArabe":"فَيَذَرُهَا قَاعًا صَفْصَفًا","tradPropre":"et les laissera comme une plaine dénudée","tradEn":"And He will leave it [i.e., the earth] a level plain;","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il ne restera alors qu’une terre plane qui les portait et cette terre sera dépourvue de plantes et de constructions.","explicationEn":"106. He will then leave the earth which used to carry them as flat, with no buildings or vegetation on it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020106","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-105.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-107.html"},{"numVerset":107,"texteArabe":"لَا تَرَىٰ فِيهَا عِوَجًا وَلَا أَمْتًا","tradPropre":"dans laquelle tu ne verras ni tortuosité, ni dépression.","tradEn":"You will not see therein a depression or an elevation.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô toi qui la verra, tu n’apercevras aucune élévation ni aucune dépression sur cette Terre aplanie.","explicationEn":"107. O onlooker, you will not see on the earth, due to it being totally flat, any curve, elevation or dip.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020107","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-106.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-108.html"},{"numVerset":108,"texteArabe":"يَوْمَئِذٍ يَتَّبِعُونَ الدَّاعِيَ لَا عِوَجَ لَهُ  وَخَشَعَتِ الْأَصْوَاتُ لِلرَّحْمَانِ فَلَا تَسْمَعُ إِلَّا هَمْسًا","tradPropre":"Ce jour-là, ils suivront le Convocateur sans tortuosité; et les voix baisseront devant le Tout Miséricordieux. Tu n'entendras alors qu'un chuchotement.","tradEn":"That Day, they [i.e., everyone] will follow [the call of] the Caller [with] no deviation therefrom, and [all] voices will be stilled before the Most Merciful, so you will not hear except a whisper [of footsteps].","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ou : de légers bruits de pas.","explicationUnanime":"Les gens suivront la voix de celui qui les appellera au rassemblement et ils n’auront d’autre choix que de le suivre. Toutes les voix se tairont par crainte du Tout Miséricordieux et tu n’entendras que de légers bruits.","explicationEn":"108. On that day, people will follow the sound of the caller towards the gathering place. There will be nothing to divert them from following it. The voices will silence for the Merciful, out of fear, so you will not hear on this day except whispering.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020108","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-107.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-109.html"},{"numVerset":109,"texteArabe":"يَوْمَئِذٍ لَا تَنْفَعُ الشَّفَاعَةُ إِلَّا مَنْ أَذِنَ لَهُ الرَّحْمَانُ وَرَضِيَ لَهُ قَوْلًا","tradPropre":"Ce jour-là, l'intercession ne profitera qu'à celui auquel le Tout Miséricordieux aura donné Sa permission et dont Il agréera la parole.","tradEn":"That Day, no intercession will benefit except [that of] one to whom the Most Merciful has given permission and has accepted his word.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Durant ce Jour terrible, aucune intercession n’aura d’effet sauf si Allah l’autorise à son auteur et agrée ce qu’il dira.","explicationEn":"109. On this great day, no intercession from any intercessor will benefit, except one whom Allah allows to intercede and Allah is pleased with what he says in intercession.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020109","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-108.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-110.html"},{"numVerset":110,"texteArabe":"يَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ وَلَا يُحِيطُونَ بِهِ عِلْمًا","tradPropre":"Il connaît ce qui est devant eux et ce qui est derrière eux, alors qu'eux-mêmes ne Le cernent pas de leur science.","tradEn":"He [i.e., Allāh] knows what is [presently] before them and what will be after them, but they do not encompass it [i.e., what He knows] in knowledge.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Leur avenir comme leur passé, selon nombre d’exégètes.","explicationUnanime":"Allah sait ce que vivront les gens lorsque surviendra l’Heure et sait aussi ce qu’ils vivent dans le bas monde tandis que Ses serviteurs n’ont aucune connaissance de Son Etre et de Ses attributs.","explicationEn":"110. Allah knows what people will face in the final hour and He knows what they will have left behind in their worldly life. All the servants together cannot encompass the knowledge of Allah’s being and His qualities.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020110","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-109.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-111.html"},{"numVerset":111,"texteArabe":"۞ وَعَنَتِ الْوُجُوهُ لِلْحَيِّ الْقَيُّومِ  وَقَدْ خَابَ مَنْ حَمَلَ ظُلْمًا","tradPropre":"Et les visages s'humilieront devant Le Vivant, Celui qui subsiste par Lui-même «al-Qayyûm», et malheureux sera celui qui [se présentera devant Lui] chargé d'une iniquité.","tradEn":"And [all] faces will be humbled before the Ever-Living, the Self-Sustaining. And he will have failed who carries injustice.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les visages des serviteurs s’humilieront devant le Vivant qui ne meurt pas, Celui qui gère les affaires de Ses serviteurs et leur donne le cours qu’Il veut. Ceux qui se seront chargés de péchés seront perdants puisqu’ils se seront exposés eux-mêmes à l’anéantissement.","explicationEn":"111. The faces of the servants will humble and surrender before the Eternal One who does not die and who takes care of the affairs of His servants by managing and administering them. And the one Who carried sin has lost, due to his taking himself to places of destruction.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020111","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-110.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-112.html"},{"numVerset":112,"texteArabe":"وَمَنْ يَعْمَلْ مِنَ الصَّالِحَاتِ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَلَا يَخَافُ ظُلْمًا وَلَا هَضْمًا","tradPropre":"Et quiconque aura fait de bonnes œuvres tout en étant croyant, ne craindra ni injustice ni oppression.","tradEn":"But he who does of righteous deeds while he is a believer - he will neither fear injustice nor deprivation.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Rien ne sera ajouté à leurs mauvaises actions.<br><br><strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Rien ne sera enlevé à leurs bonnes œuvres.","explicationUnanime":"Quiconque accomplit de bonnes œuvres tout en croyant en Allah et en Ses messagers obtiendra la totalité de sa rétribution et il n’aura pas à craindre d’être injustement châtié pour un péché qu’il n’a pas commis ni que l’on diminue une part de la récompense méritée pour ses bonnes œuvres.","explicationEn":"112. Whoever does good deeds whilst believing in Allah and His messengers will attain his full reward, and will neither fear injustice by being punished for a sin he did not commit nor a decrease in the reward of his good deeds.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020112","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-111.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-113.html"},{"numVerset":113,"texteArabe":"وَكَذَالِكَ أَنْزَلْنَاهُ قُرْآنًا عَرَبِيًّا وَصَرَّفْنَا فِيهِ مِنَ الْوَعِيدِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُونَ أَوْ يُحْدِثُ لَهُمْ ذِكْرًا","tradPropre":"C'est ainsi que nous l'avons fait descendre un Coran en [langue] arabe, et Nous y avons multiplié les menaces, afin qu'ils deviennent pieux ou qu'il les incite à s'exhorter?","tradEn":"And thus We have sent it down as an Arabic Qur’ān and have diversified therein the warnings that perhaps they will avoid [sin] or it would cause them remembrance.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tout comme Nous révélons les récits des anciens, Nous révélons ce Coran en une langue arabe claire et y exposons de multiples menaces et avertissements afin que, peut-être, ils craignent Allah et tirent des leçons du Coran.","explicationEn":"113. I have revealed the Qur’ān in clear Arabic just as I revealed the stories of the previous prophets, and I have explained in it different warnings of threat and fear, in the hope they will fear Allah or that the admonition of the Qur’ān will cause them to reflect.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020113","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-112.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-114.html"},{"numVerset":114,"texteArabe":"فَتَعَالَى اللَّهُ الْمَلِكُ الْحَقُّ  وَلَا تَعْجَلْ بِالْقُرْآنِ مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ يُقْضَىٰ إِلَيْكَ وَحْيُهُ  وَقُلْ رَبِّ زِدْنِي عِلْمًا","tradPropre":"Que soit éxalté Allah, le Vrai Souverain! Ne te hâte pas [de réciter] le Coran avant que ne te soit achevée sa révélation. Et dis: «O mon Seigneur, accroît mes connaissances!»","tradEn":"So high [above all] is Allāh, the Sovereign, the Truth. And, [O Muḥammad], do not hasten with [recitation of] the Qur’ān before its revelation is completed to you, and say, \"My Lord, increase me in knowledge.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Mais garde le silence jusqu’au moment où l’ange Gabriel aura fini de te le réciter, alors seulement tu pourras le répéter après lui, sans craindre de l’oublier.","explicationUnanime":"Qu’Allah soit donc élevé et sanctifié! Il est le Roi dont la souveraineté s’étend à toute chose et la Vérité dont la parole est toute vérité. Qu’il soit élevé au-dessus de ce que Lui attribuent les polythéistes. Ô Messager, ne t’empresse pas de réciter le Coran de concert avec Gabriel avant qu’il ne t’ait transmis la totalité des versets révélés et dis: Ô Seigneur, ajoute davantage de connaissances à celles que je détiens déjà.","explicationEn":"114. Allah is High above and Exalted from what the idolaters describe Him with of deficiencies and from what they attribute as partners to Him. He is the Majestic King, to whom belongs the kingdom of everything, and who is the Truth and speaks the truth. Do not hasten, O Messenger, in reciting the Qur’ān with Gabriel before it is completely conveyed to you, and say: O Lord, increase me in knowledge, on top of what You have already taught me.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020114","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-113.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-115.html"},{"numVerset":115,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ عَهِدْنَا إِلَىٰ آدَمَ مِنْ قَبْلُ فَنَسِيَ وَلَمْ نَجِدْ لَهُ عَزْمًا","tradPropre":"En effet, Nous avons auparavant fait une recommandation à Adam; mais il oublia; et Nous n'avons pas trouvé chez lui de résolution ferme.","tradEn":"And We had already taken a promise from Adam before, but he forgot; and We found not in him determination.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Celui de ne pas manger des fruits de l’arbre défendu, selon nombre d’exégètes.","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons auparavant fait une recommandation à Adam: celle de ne pas manger des fruits de l’arbre défendu et l’avons informé des conséquences s’il désobéissait. Seulement, il oublia cette recommandation et ne put se retenir de manger des fruits de cet arbre. Il n’avait en effet pas pris la ferme résolution d’obéir.","explicationEn":"115. And I enjoined on Adam beforehand not to eat of the tree, and I forbade him from this and explained to him its consequences. But he forgot the instruction, ate of the tree and was unable to resist it. And I did not see in him resolve to observe what I enjoined.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020115","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-114.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-116.html"},{"numVerset":116,"texteArabe":"وَإِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ اسْجُدُوا لِآدَمَ فَسَجَدُوا إِلَّا إِبْلِيسَ أَبَىٰ","tradPropre":"Et quand Nous dîmes aux Anges: «Prosternez-vous devant Adam», ils se prosternèrent, excepté Iblis qui refusa.","tradEn":"And [mention] when We said to the angels, \"Prostrate to Adam,\" and they prostrated, except Iblees; he refused.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, rappelle-toi lorsque Nous dîmes aux anges: Prosternez-vous devant Adam en guise de salutation. Tous se prosternèrent, excepté Iblîs qui était présent mais qui n’est pas un ange. Poussé par son orgueil, il refusa de se prosterner.","explicationEn":"116. And remember, O Messenger, when I said to the angels: “Prostrate to Adam as a greeting”. All of them prostrated besides Iblis, who was with them but not from them. He refused to prostrate out of arrogance.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020116","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-115.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-117.html"},{"numVerset":117,"texteArabe":"فَقُلْنَا يَا آدَمُ إِنَّ هَاذَا عَدُوٌّ لَكَ وَلِزَوْجِكَ فَلَا يُخْرِجَنَّكُمَا مِنَ الْجَنَّةِ فَتَشْقَىٰ","tradPropre":"Alors Nous dîmes: «O Adam, celui-là est vraiment un ennemi pour toi et ton épouse. Prenez garde qu'il vous fasse sortir du Paradis, car alors tu seras malheureux.","tradEn":"So We said, \"O Adam, indeed this is an enemy to you and to your wife. Then let him not remove you from Paradise so you would suffer.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous dîmes alors: Ô Adam, Iblîs est ton ennemi et celui de ton épouse. Qu’il ne vous fasse pas sortir du Paradis par ses insufflations, tu subirais alors les conséquences d’avoir obéi à ce qu’il vous insuffle.","explicationEn":"117. So I said: “O Adam, Iblis is your enemy and your wife’s enemy, so let him not take you and your wife out of paradise, by obeying him in what he whispers, in which case you will bear difficulties and hardship.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020117","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-116.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-118.html"},{"numVerset":118,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ لَكَ أَلَّا تَجُوعَ فِيهَا وَلَا تَعْرَىٰ","tradPropre":"Car tu n'y auras pas faim ni ne seras nu,","tradEn":"Indeed, it is [promised] for you not to be hungry therein or be unclothed.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Dans le Paradis, Allah se charge de te préserver de la faim en te nourrissant et de te préserver de la nudité en te vêtissant.","explicationEn":"118. It is Allah’s responsibility towards you that He will feed you, so you will not get hungry, and to clothe you, so you will not be naked.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020118","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-117.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-119.html"},{"numVerset":119,"texteArabe":"وَأَنَّكَ لَا تَظْمَأُ فِيهَا وَلَا تَضْحَىٰ","tradPropre":"tu n'y auras pas soif ni ne seras frappé par l'ardeur du soleil».","tradEn":"And indeed, you will not be thirsty therein or be hot from the sun.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il se charge aussi de te préserver de la soif en t’abreuvant et de préserver de la chaleur du soleil en t’abritant.","explicationEn":"119. And to give you water so that you do not get thirsty, and to shade you so that the heat of the sun does not affect you”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020119","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-118.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-120.html"},{"numVerset":120,"texteArabe":"فَوَسْوَسَ إِلَيْهِ الشَّيْطَانُ قَالَ يَا آدَمُ هَلْ أَدُلُّكَ عَلَىٰ شَجَرَةِ الْخُلْدِ وَمُلْكٍ لَا يَبْلَىٰ","tradPropre":"Puis le Diable le tenta en disant: «O Adam, t'indiquerai-je l'arbre de l'éternité et un royaume impérissable?»","tradEn":"Then Satan whispered to him; he said, \"O Adam, shall I direct you to the tree of eternity and possession that will not deteriorate?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est alors que Satan insuffla à Adam ce qui suit: Veux-tu que je te montre un arbre qui, si tu mangeais de ses fruits, te permettrait de ne jamais mourir, te ferait vivre pour l’éternité, et te mettrait à la tête d’un royaume invincible.","explicationEn":"120. But the satan whispered to Adam saying: “Shall I show you a tree that whoever eats from it will never die, but in fact remain forever, and possess an everlasting kingdom that will never break or end?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020120","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-119.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-121.html"},{"numVerset":121,"texteArabe":"فَأَكَلَا مِنْهَا فَبَدَتْ لَهُمَا سَوْآتُهُمَا وَطَفِقَا يَخْصِفَانِ عَلَيْهِمَا مِنْ وَرَقِ الْجَنَّةِ  وَعَصَىٰ آدَمُ رَبَّهُ فَغَوَىٰ","tradPropre":"Tous deux (Adam et Eve) en mangèrent. Alors leur apparut leur nudité. Ils se mirent à se couvrir avec des feuilles du paradis. Adam désobéit ainsi à son Seigneur et il s'égara.","tradEn":"And they [i.e., Adam and his wife] ate of it, and their private parts became apparent to them, and they began to fasten over themselves from the leaves of Paradise. And Adam disobeyed his Lord and erred.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Adam et Eve mangèrent alors des fruits de l’arbre qui leur avait été défendu et ils prirent conscience de leur nudité. Ils se mirent à la couvrir à l’aide des feuilles des arbres du Paradis. C’est ainsi qu’Adam désobéit à l’ordre de son Seigneur et outrepassa la limite de ce qui lui était permis.","explicationEn":"121. Then Adam and Eve ate of the tree they were forbidden to eat from, then their private areas became exposed to them after they were hidden, and they began to pluck the leaves of the trees of paradise and cover their private areas with them. Adam opposed the command of his Lord, as he did not comply with His order of refraining from eating of the tree, and so he trespassed the bounds towards that which was not allowed for him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020121","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-120.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-122.html"},{"numVerset":122,"texteArabe":"ثُمَّ اجْتَبَاهُ رَبُّهُ فَتَابَ عَلَيْهِ وَهَدَىٰ","tradPropre":"Son Seigneur l'a ensuite élu, agréé son repentir et l'a guidé.","tradEn":"Then his Lord chose him and turned to him in forgiveness and guided [him].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis Allah l’a élu, accepta son repentir et lui facilita de se guider dans le droit chemin.","explicationEn":"122. Then Allah chose him, accepted his repentance and enabled him to be guided.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020122","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-121.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-123.html"},{"numVerset":123,"texteArabe":"قَالَ اهْبِطَا مِنْهَا جَمِيعًا  بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ  فَإِمَّا يَأْتِيَنَّكُمْ مِنِّي هُدًى فَمَنِ اتَّبَعَ هُدَايَ فَلَا يَضِلُّ وَلَا يَشْقَىٰ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «Descendez d'ici, (Adam et Eve), [Vous serez] tous (avec vos descendants) ennemis les uns des autres. Puis, si jamais un guide vous vient de Ma part, quiconque suit Mon guide ne s'égarera ni ne sera malheureux.","tradEn":"[Allāh] said, \"Descend from it [i.e., Paradise] - all, [your descendants] being enemies to one another. And if there should come to you guidance from Me - then whoever follows My guidance will neither go astray [in the world] nor suffer [in the Hereafter].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ensuite, Allah dit à Adam et à Eve: Descendez, vous et Iblîs, du Paradis. Il sera votre ennemi et vous serez les siens. Quand vous parviendra un appel à Ma guidée: celui qui le suit et le met en pratique sans en dévier ne s’égarera pas de la vérité ni ne sera malheureux dans l’au-delà. Et au lieu d’entrer en Enfer, il entrera plutôt au Paradis.","explicationEn":"123. Allah said to Adam and Eve: “Both of you and Iblis, descend from paradise, because he is your enemy and you are his enemies. If there comes to you from Me an explanation of My path, then whoever amongst you follows the explanation of my path, acts accordingly and does not divert from it, he will not go astray from the truth nor will he be misfortunate in the afterlife through punishment, but rather Allah will enter him into paradise.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020123","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-122.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-124.html"},{"numVerset":124,"texteArabe":"وَمَنْ أَعْرَضَ عَنْ ذِكْرِي فَإِنَّ لَهُ مَعِيشَةً ضَنْكًا وَنَحْشُرُهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ أَعْمَىٰ","tradPropre":"Et quiconque se détourne de Mon Rappel, mènera certes, une vie pleine de gêne, et le Jour de la Résurrection Nous l'amènerons aveugle au rassemblement».","tradEn":"And whoever turns away from My remembrance - indeed, he will have a depressed [i.e., difficult] life, and We will gather [i.e., raise] him on the Day of Resurrection blind.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tandis que celui qui se détournera de Mon Rappel et n’y répondra pas favorablement, il mènera une vie pénible dans le bas monde et dans le monde intermédiaire. De plus, Nous le convoquerons au Rassemblement après l’avoir rendu aveugle et dépourvu d’argument.","explicationEn":"124. And whoever turns away from My reminder and does not accept it or respond to it shall have a constricted and miserable life in this world and in the Transitory Stage, and I shall lead him towards the gathering place on the Day of Judgment without eyesight and proof.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020124","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-123.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-125.html"},{"numVerset":125,"texteArabe":"قَالَ رَبِّ لِمَ حَشَرْتَنِي أَعْمَىٰ وَقَدْ كُنْتُ بَصِيرًا","tradPropre":"Il dira: «O mon Seigneur, pourquoi m'as-Tu amené aveugle alors qu'auparavant je voyais?»","tradEn":"He will say, \"My Lord, why have you raised me blind while I was [once] seeing?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Cet homme dira: Ô Seigneur, tu m’as rendu aveugle alors que j’étais voyant dans le bas monde.","explicationEn":"125. This person will say: “O Lord, why did you raise me blind today when I could see in the world?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020125","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-124.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-126.html"},{"numVerset":126,"texteArabe":"قَالَ كَذَالِكَ أَتَتْكَ آيَاتُنَا فَنَسِيتَهَا  وَكَذَالِكَ الْيَوْمَ تُنْسَىٰ","tradPropre":"[Allah lui] dira: «De même que Nos Signes (enseignements) t'étaient venus et que tu les as oubliés, ainsi aujourd'hui tu es oublié».","tradEn":"[Allāh] will say, \"Thus did Our signs come to you, and you forgot [i.e., disregarded] them; and thus will you this Day be forgotten.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Allah répondra à cet homme: Tout comme tu as dédaigné et délaissé nos signes dans le bas monde, tu seras délaissé aujourd’hui et abandonné au châtiment.","explicationEn":"126. Allah said in refutation of him: “This is like what you did in the world, because My signs came to you but you turned away from them and left them. Likewise, you will be left today in punishment”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020126","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-125.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-127.html"},{"numVerset":127,"texteArabe":"وَكَذَالِكَ نَجْزِي مَنْ أَسْرَفَ وَلَمْ يُؤْمِنْ بِآيَاتِ رَبِّهِ  وَلَعَذَابُ الْآخِرَةِ أَشَدُّ وَأَبْقَىٰ","tradPropre":"Ainsi sanctionnons-nous l'outrancier qui ne croit pas aux révélations de son Seigneur. Et certes, le châtiment de l'au-delà est plus sévère et plus durable.","tradEn":"And thus do We recompense he who transgressed and did not believe in the signs of his Lord. And the punishment of the Hereafter is more severe and more enduring.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"C’est ainsi que Nous rétribuons celui qui est absorbé par les plaisirs illicites et refuse de croire aux indices clairs lui provenant de son Seigneur. Le châtiment d’Allah dans l’au-delà sera plus horrible encore, plus sévère et plus durable que la vie pénible du bas monde et de la vie intermédiaire.","explicationEn":"127. And this is the kind of reward I give to the one engrossed in unlawful desires and who turns away from believing in the clear proofs from his Lord. And the punishment of Allah in the Hearafter is even more horrible, severe, and lasting, than the life they will have in the world and in the transition.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020127","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-126.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-128.html"},{"numVerset":128,"texteArabe":"أَفَلَمْ يَهْدِ لَهُمْ كَمْ أَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِنَ الْقُرُونِ يَمْشُونَ فِي مَسَاكِنِهِمْ  إِنَّ فِي ذَالِكَ لَآيَاتٍ لِأُولِي النُّهَىٰ","tradPropre":"Cela ne leur a-t-il pas servi de direction, que Nous ayons fait périr avant eux tant de générations dans les demeures desquelles ils marchent maintenant? Voilà bien là des leçons pour les doués d'intelligence!","tradEn":"Then, has it not become clear to them how many generations We destroyed before them as they walk among their dwellings? Indeed in that are signs for those of intelligence.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les polythéistes n’ont-ils pas acquis la certitude que Nous avons anéanti de nombreux peuples avant eux? Ils déambulent pourtant entre les demeures de ces peuples et voient de leurs yeux leurs ruines! L’anéantissement et la destruction de ces nombreux peuples représentent des enseignements adressés à ceux qui sont doués de raison.","explicationEn":"128. Is it not clear to the idolaters how many nations I destroyed before them? They walk in the homes of these destroyed nations and see the effects of what befell them. In the destruction and ruination which befell these many nations are lessons for people of intelligence.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020128","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-127.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-129.html"},{"numVerset":129,"texteArabe":"وَلَوْلَا كَلِمَةٌ سَبَقَتْ مِنْ رَبِّكَ لَكَانَ لِزَامًا وَأَجَلٌ مُسَمًّى","tradPropre":"N'eussent-été un décret préalable de ton Seigneur et aussi un terme déjà fixé, (leur châtiment) aurait été inévitable (et immédiat).","tradEn":"And if not for a word that preceded from your Lord, it [i.e., punishment] would have been an obligation [due immediately], and [if not for] a specified term [decreed].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, si Allah n’avait pas décrété qu’Il ne châtierait personne avant de lui avoir explicité Son argument, Il se serait hâté de châtier ces polythéistes qui le méritent.","explicationEn":"129. O Messenger, had a word not preceded from your Lord that He will not punish anyone before establishing the proof against him, and had there not been a time which is fixed with Him, the punishment would have come to them quickly, due to their deserving it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020129","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-128.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-130.html"},{"numVerset":130,"texteArabe":"فَاصْبِرْ عَلَىٰ مَا يَقُولُونَ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ قَبْلَ طُلُوعِ الشَّمْسِ وَقَبْلَ غُرُوبِهَا  وَمِنْ آنَاءِ اللَّيْلِ فَسَبِّحْ وَأَطْرَافَ النَّهَارِ لَعَلَّكَ تَرْضَىٰ","tradPropre":"Supporte patiemment ce qu'ils disent et célèbre Sa louange, avant le lever du soleil, avant son coucher et pendant la nuit; et exalte Sa Gloire aux extrémités du jour. Peut-être auras-tu satisfaction:","tradEn":"So be patient over what they say and exalt [Allāh] with praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting; and during periods of the night [exalt Him] and at the ends of the day, that you may be satisfied.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> De la récompense qui te sera accordée si tu accomplis les œuvres mentionnées ici et qui, selon la majorité des exégètes, sont les cinq prières quotidiennes.","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, endure patiemment les médisances des dénégateurs et célèbre la louange de ton Seigneur durant la prière de l’aube avant le lever du soleil, durant la prière de l’après-midi, durant la prière du coucher du soleil, durant la prière du soir lorsqu’il fait nuit et durant la prière de midi lorsque le soleil dépasse son zénith. Célèbre Sa louange aussi lorsque le jour commence et finit afin d’obtenir d’Allah la récompense qui te satisfait.","explicationEn":"130. So be patient, O Messenger, on the false things those who disbelieve in you say about you. Glorify and praise your Lord in the Fajr prayer before sunrise; in the Asr prayer before sunset; in the hours of night in the Maghrib and Isha prayers; and in the Zuhr prayer just after the zenith, which is the end of the first part of the day and the beginning of the second part; in the hope of attaining reward with Allah which you will be pleased with.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020130","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-129.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-131.html"},{"numVerset":131,"texteArabe":"وَلَا تَمُدَّنَّ عَيْنَيْكَ إِلَىٰ مَا مَتَّعْنَا بِهِ أَزْوَاجًا مِنْهُمْ زَهْرَةَ الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا لِنَفْتِنَهُمْ فِيهِ  وَرِزْقُ رَبِّكَ خَيْرٌ وَأَبْقَىٰ","tradPropre":"Et ne tends point les yeux vers ce dont Nous avons donné jouissance temporaire à certains groupes d'entre eux, comme décor de la vie présente, afin de les éprouver par cela. Ce qu'Allah fournit (au Paradis) est meilleur et plus durable.","tradEn":"And do not extend your eyes toward that by which We have given enjoyment to [some] categories of them, [its being but] the splendor of worldly life by which We test them. And the provision of your Lord is better and more enduring.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ne regarde pas les plaisirs de ce bas monde dont Nous laissons les dénégateurs jouir afin de les éprouver car ce que Nous leur accordons est éphémère tandis que la récompense que te promet ton Seigneur afin de te satisfaire est meilleure et plus durable. Elle ne s’interrompra jamais.","explicationEn":"131. And do not desire the types of enjoyment I have given to different groups of the disbelievers, the glitter of the worldly life which they enjoy so that I may test them. What I have given them of this will disappear, and the reward of your Lord which He has promised you and which will make you pleased is better and more lasting.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020131","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-130.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-132.html"},{"numVerset":132,"texteArabe":"وَأْمُرْ أَهْلَكَ بِالصَّلَاةِ وَاصْطَبِرْ عَلَيْهَا  لَا نَسْأَلُكَ رِزْقًا  نَحْنُ نَرْزُقُكَ  وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِلتَّقْوَىٰ","tradPropre":"Et commande à ta famille la Salât, et fais-la avec persévérance. Nous ne te demandons point de nourriture: c'est à Nous de te nourrir. La bonne fin est réservée à la piété.","tradEn":"And enjoin prayer upon your family [and people] and be steadfast therein. We ask you not for provision; We provide for you, and the [best] outcome is for [those of] righteousness.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Et celle des hommes et n’attendons de toi aucune offrande.","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, ordonne à ta famille d’accomplir la prière et efforce-toi d’y être persévérant. Nous ne te demandons ni à toi ni à quiconque de te pourvoir car Nous nous chargeons de ta subsistance et la fin heureuse dans ce bas monde et dans l’au-delà sera pour les pieux qui craignent Allah en se conformant à Ses commandements et en renonçant à Ses interdits.","explicationEn":"132. And order your family, O Messenger, to perform prayer, and you also remain constant in its performance. I do not ask you for your own sustenance or that of others; I will take care of your sustenance. The praiseworthy outcome in this world and the afterlife is for the pious who fear Allah, carrying out His commands and refraining from His prohibitions.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020132","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-131.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-133.html"},{"numVerset":133,"texteArabe":"وَقَالُوا لَوْلَا يَأْتِينَا بِآيَةٍ مِنْ رَبِّهِ  أَوَلَمْ تَأْتِهِمْ بَيِّنَةُ مَا فِي الصُّحُفِ الْأُولَىٰ","tradPropre":"Et ils disent: «Pourquoi ne nous apporte-t-il pas un miracle de son Seigneur? La Preuve (le Coran) de ce que contiennent les Ecritures anciennes ne leur est-elle pas venue?","tradEn":"And they say, \"Why does he not bring us a sign from his Lord?\" Has there not come to them evidence of what was in the former scriptures?","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ou : un prophète annoncé par ces mêmes Ecritures.","explicationUnanime":"Ces mécréants qui démentent le Prophète lui disent: Si Muħammad nous apportais de son Seigneur un signe démontrant qu’il dit vrai lorsqu’il prétend être un messager? Ces dénégateurs n’ont-ils pas reçu le Coran qui confirme les livres révélés par le passé?","explicationEn":"133. These disbelievers who reject the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Why does Muhammad not bring us a sign from his Lord which proves his truthfulness and that he is a Messenger?” Has the Qur’ān which confirms the previous divine books not come to these rejecters?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020133","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-132.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-134.html"},{"numVerset":134,"texteArabe":"وَلَوْ أَنَّا أَهْلَكْنَاهُمْ بِعَذَابٍ مِنْ قَبْلِهِ لَقَالُوا رَبَّنَا لَوْلَا أَرْسَلْتَ إِلَيْنَا رَسُولًا فَنَتَّبِعَ آيَاتِكَ مِنْ قَبْلِ أَنْ نَذِلَّ وَنَخْزَىٰ","tradPropre":"Et si Nous les avions fait périr par un châtiment avant lui [Muhammad], ils auraient certainement dit: «O notre Seigneur, pourquoi ne nous as-Tu pas envoyé de Messager? Nous aurions alors suivi Tes enseignements avant d'avoir été humiliés et jetés dans l'ignominie».","tradEn":"And if We had destroyed them with a punishment before him, they would have said, \"Our Lord, why did You not send to us a messenger so we could have followed Your verses [i.e., teachings] before we were humiliated and disgraced?\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> De Mouhammad ou la révélation du Coran.<br><br><strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Le Jour dernier, précisent nombre de commentateurs.","explicationUnanime":"Si Nous avions anéantis ces mécréants qui démentent le Prophète et les avions châtiés pour leur entêtement à mécroire avant même de leur envoyer un messager et de leur révéler un livre, ils auraient justifié leur mécréance le Jour de la Résurrection en ces termes: Ô notre Seigneur, pourquoi ne pas nous avoir envoyé un messager dans le bas monde? Nous aurions alors cru en lui et aurions accordé du crédit aux signes qu’il nous aurait apporté avant que Ton châtiment ne nous couvre d’opprobre.","explicationEn":"134. And if I were to destroy these deniers of the Prophet (peace be upon him) by sending punishment on them due to their disbelief and obstinacy, before sending a messenger to them and revealing a book to them, they would say on the Day of Judgment, as an excuse for their disbelief: “O Lord, if only You had sent a messenger to us in the world, so that we could have believed in him and followed the verses that he brought, before disgrace and shame befell us through Your punishment”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020134","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-133.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-20-verset-135.html"},{"numVerset":135,"texteArabe":"قُلْ كُلٌّ مُتَرَبِّصٌ فَتَرَبَّصُوا  فَسَتَعْلَمُونَ مَنْ أَصْحَابُ الصِّرَاطِ السَّوِيِّ وَمَنِ اهْتَدَىٰ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Chacun attend. Attendez donc! Vous saurez bientôt qui sont les gens du droit chemin et qui sont les bien-guidés».","tradEn":"Say, \"Each [of us] is waiting; so wait. For you will know who are the companions of the sound path and who is guided.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, dis à ces dénégateurs: Chacun de nous et de vous est dans l’attente de ce que décrète Allah. Attendez donc et vous saurez certainement qui de nous ou de vous est sur le droit chemin et a été guidé.","explicationEn":"135. O Messenger, say to these deniers: “Each one of us and you awaits what Allah will carry out, so wait. You will most certainly come to know who are the people of the straight path and who are the guided: us or you?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"020135","lienPrecedent":"sourate-20-verset-134.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-21-verset-1.html"}]};